WEBVTT

00:00:17.627 --> 00:00:23.260
The ghosts of Eddington Castle.

00:00:23.319 --> 00:00:29.962
Eddington Castle on the border of England and Scotland.

00:00:30.022 --> 00:00:34.324
The year is 1605.

00:00:34.384 --> 00:00:37.345
Holt!

00:00:37.405 --> 00:00:38.676
Who goes there?

00:00:38.736 --> 00:00:39.466
Let us in.

00:00:39.526 --> 00:00:40.556
We have a prisoner.

00:00:40.616 --> 00:00:41.717
Who is this man?

00:00:41.777 --> 00:00:43.118
Robert McKenzie.

00:00:43.178 --> 00:00:44.158
He's a traitor.

00:00:44.218 --> 00:00:45.318
He has to be hanged.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.128
Place him in the dungeon.

00:00:47.188 --> 00:00:48.717
Take him to the dungeon.

00:00:48.737 --> 00:00:50.968
Get up, Mackenzie.

00:00:51.028 --> 00:00:54.060
Take your hands off me, you English pig.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.412
Why you?

00:00:56.472 --> 00:00:59.022
Put your sword away.

00:00:59.082 --> 00:01:04.835
He will be hanged as every traitor should be, and then his body will be thrown from the castle walls.

00:01:04.896 --> 00:01:07.737
Take him to the dungeon.

00:01:07.797 --> 00:01:14.135
Put him in there.

00:01:14.195 --> 00:01:26.094
The following night, the night before Robert Mackenzie was due to be hanged, a hay wagon arrived at the gates of the castle.

00:01:26.154 --> 00:01:27.825
Oops.

00:01:27.885 --> 00:01:29.115
Who goes there?

00:01:29.175 --> 00:01:30.456
Gabriel West.

00:01:30.516 --> 00:01:32.146
What is your business here?

00:01:32.206 --> 00:01:33.176
You know me.

00:01:33.236 --> 00:01:34.927
I'll bring hay for your horses.

00:01:34.987 --> 00:01:35.937
Wait.

00:01:35.997 --> 00:01:37.878
Let me look.

00:01:37.938 --> 00:01:40.038
Can I go in now?

00:01:40.098 --> 00:01:41.369
You may pass.

00:01:41.428 --> 00:01:42.439
Thank you.

00:01:42.499 --> 00:01:44.480
Get up!

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.750
Whoa!

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.760
What did you do now?

00:01:49.819 --> 00:01:51.300
Stand still.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.011
Wait a minute.

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:54.302
What?

00:01:54.361 --> 00:01:59.824
Who's that?

00:01:59.884 --> 00:02:01.945
Don't say a word.

00:02:02.005 --> 00:02:03.126
Who are you?

00:02:03.185 --> 00:02:04.796
And how did you get into my wagon?

00:02:04.856 --> 00:02:06.117
Don't ask questions.

00:02:06.177 --> 00:02:07.478
I will call for help.

00:02:07.538 --> 00:02:09.518
If you do anything, I will kill you.

00:02:09.538 --> 00:02:11.454
No, stop.

00:02:11.514 --> 00:02:13.141
What do you want from me?

00:02:13.201 --> 00:02:15.603
Tell me where the dungeons are.

00:02:15.663 --> 00:02:18.946
I don't know where the dungeons are.

00:02:19.006 --> 00:02:22.829
Can you feel the blade of my knife on your throat?

00:02:22.889 --> 00:02:23.740
Alright!

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.472
I will kill you if you don't do as I say.

00:02:26.532 --> 00:02:27.474
Stop!

00:02:27.533 --> 00:02:30.296
Where are the dungeons?

00:02:30.356 --> 00:02:33.088
On the other side of this courtyard.

00:02:33.148 --> 00:02:34.400
Right.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.300
Now listen to me.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.255
Unload your hay and wait here.

00:02:39.315 --> 00:03:11.138
back in five minutes I intend to leave the castle in your wagon I should I wait for you because if you don't I will kill you and why does to stop me leaving the castle without you before you come back I have friends outside the castle waiting for this wagon if I am not on it they will kill you I will do as you ask but why do you want to go to the dungeons my husband is there your husband The traitor Robert McKenzie is your husband.

00:03:11.198 --> 00:03:14.035
Don't dare use the word traitor in front of me again.

00:03:14.055 --> 00:03:17.492
Don't tell me again.

00:03:17.552 --> 00:03:19.594
Where are the dungeons?

00:03:19.653 --> 00:03:22.656
Across the courtyard, and then down some steps.

00:03:22.716 --> 00:03:23.516
Thank you.

00:03:23.576 --> 00:03:24.958
But you'll never get there.

00:03:25.018 --> 00:03:25.718
Why not?

00:03:25.778 --> 00:03:29.071
There is a guard at the top of the steps and another at the bottom.

00:03:29.131 --> 00:03:30.642
They will not be a problem.

00:03:30.702 --> 00:03:33.706
Just make sure you are ready to leave when I return.

00:03:33.766 --> 00:03:39.591
And if you breathe a word to these guards, you will die an ugly death when you leave this castle.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.002
I understand.

00:03:42.062 --> 00:03:47.492
I'm not waiting for you, you dangerous witch.

00:03:47.552 --> 00:03:49.997
God.

00:03:50.057 --> 00:03:51.248
Who's there?

00:03:51.308 --> 00:03:52.988
It is me.

00:03:53.048 --> 00:03:53.968
Who?

00:03:54.028 --> 00:03:55.159
Who is it?

00:03:55.219 --> 00:03:57.360
Come closer.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:05.992
Who are you and what?

00:04:06.052 --> 00:04:08.913
Who goes there?

00:04:08.972 --> 00:04:15.929
Adam, is it you?

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:22.586
Who's there?

00:04:22.645 --> 00:04:24.157
Is it time?

00:04:24.217 --> 00:04:25.438
Robert!

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.929
It is me!

00:04:26.988 --> 00:04:28.050
Elizabeth!

00:04:28.109 --> 00:04:28.890
Yes!

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.662
Oh my God, let me hold you!

00:04:31.722 --> 00:04:35.244
Robert, quickly we must leave!

00:04:35.304 --> 00:04:35.965
Leave!

00:04:36.025 --> 00:04:36.826
Yes, come!

00:04:36.846 --> 00:04:38.517
Oh my God!

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:39.938
What have you done?

00:04:39.998 --> 00:04:41.679
Have you killed the guard?

00:04:41.739 --> 00:04:43.750
I have killed two guards.

00:04:43.809 --> 00:04:46.661
I will kill as many as it takes to free you.

00:04:46.721 --> 00:04:47.672
Now come!

00:04:47.732 --> 00:04:49.393
But how can we escape?

00:04:49.452 --> 00:04:50.753
What are we to do?

00:04:50.813 --> 00:04:53.564
But there's no time to talk.

00:04:53.624 --> 00:04:59.548
Put on this cloak and follow me.

00:04:59.608 --> 00:05:06.130
You see the wagon on the other side of the courtyard?

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:06.741
Yes.

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:08.752
We are going to escape in that.

00:05:08.812 --> 00:05:14.482
Come on.

00:05:14.542 --> 00:05:20.023
What the?

00:05:20.043 --> 00:05:21.614
The stupid fool!

00:05:21.674 --> 00:05:23.506
The wagon has gone!

00:05:23.566 --> 00:05:24.897
What's happening?

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:25.798
Quick!

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.439
There are horses over there.

00:05:27.499 --> 00:05:31.052
We can still get out before they lower the gate.

00:05:31.112 --> 00:05:32.813
Stop!

00:05:32.873 --> 00:05:34.154
Who are you?

00:05:34.214 --> 00:05:35.725
We need two horses.

00:05:35.785 --> 00:05:37.006
What?

00:05:37.066 --> 00:05:40.068
Quickly!

00:05:40.128 --> 00:05:46.339
To post the gates, the prisoner is escaping.

00:05:46.399 --> 00:05:50.247
Yes Captain, give me your crossbarrow.

00:05:50.307 --> 00:05:55.192
Yes Captain, put me your hole.

00:05:55.251 --> 00:05:56.814
Robert!

00:05:56.874 --> 00:05:58.355
Elizabeth!

00:05:58.414 --> 00:05:59.666
I've been hit!

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:00.556
Robert!

00:06:00.616 --> 00:06:02.098
Don't stop!

00:06:02.157 --> 00:06:03.670
I've been hit!

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.160
I'm dying!

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:07.742
Wait!

00:06:07.802 --> 00:06:10.746
Hold on to me.

00:06:10.806 --> 00:06:14.002
We can ride on one horse.

00:06:14.061 --> 00:06:45.310
Elizabeth save yourself leave me to die here why are you so spineless robot hold on to me Leave me, Elizabeth.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:46.930
Hold on to me, Robert.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:52.834
If we get beyond the village, we'll be in the forest and there will never catch us.

00:06:52.893 --> 00:06:55.265
I can't go on.

00:06:55.325 --> 00:06:57.816
I'm bleeding to death.

00:06:57.876 --> 00:06:58.957
Wait.

00:06:59.017 --> 00:07:00.718
There's house over there.

00:07:00.778 --> 00:07:04.360
We can get there before the English scum come over the hill.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:07.482
We will ask the people in the house to shelter us.

00:07:07.542 --> 00:07:09.042
And if they don't...

00:07:09.102 --> 00:07:13.549
If they are true, Scots, they will help us.

00:07:13.609 --> 00:07:19.515
Robert, let me help you.

00:07:19.575 --> 00:07:24.306
Lean against the wall.

00:07:24.366 --> 00:07:26.377
Go princess!

00:07:26.437 --> 00:07:27.338
Go!

00:07:27.398 --> 00:07:32.330
Run into the forest!

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:36.661
Who's there?

00:07:36.721 --> 00:07:38.301
Open the door!

00:07:38.321 --> 00:07:40.132
Who are you?

00:07:40.192 --> 00:07:42.798
Open the door, I tell you!

00:07:42.858 --> 00:07:44.694
Who are you?

00:07:44.754 --> 00:07:46.604
And who is this man?

00:07:46.664 --> 00:07:47.954
What's happened to him?

00:07:48.014 --> 00:07:49.065
Let us in.

00:07:49.125 --> 00:07:49.895
Why?

00:07:49.955 --> 00:07:51.906
The English are coming after us.

00:07:51.966 --> 00:07:53.386
Why are they after you?

00:07:53.446 --> 00:07:54.417
What have you done?

00:07:54.477 --> 00:07:56.067
You were prisoners, aren't you?

00:07:56.127 --> 00:07:58.598
You must have escaped from Eddington Castle.

00:07:58.658 --> 00:08:03.180
I won't let you and they'll kill me.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:07.041
There we are!

00:08:07.081 --> 00:08:08.152
Fire!

00:08:08.212 --> 00:08:13.222
Dear God in heaven, you are not coming in here.

00:08:13.282 --> 00:08:16.922
Oh my God!

00:08:16.982 --> 00:08:22.846
You will regret this moment until you're dying day!

00:08:22.906 --> 00:08:30.609
In the name of Scotland, I put a curse on your family for all time!

00:08:30.629 --> 00:08:36.792
Fire!

00:08:36.852 --> 00:08:38.392
Good.

00:08:38.452 --> 00:08:39.818
That was dead.

00:08:39.878 --> 00:08:42.073
Oh, God, preserve us.

00:08:42.133 --> 00:08:43.374
What is your name?

00:08:43.434 --> 00:08:45.025
Andrew McPherson.

00:08:45.085 --> 00:08:46.326
You're a Scotsman.

00:08:46.386 --> 00:08:47.726
Yes, I am.

00:08:47.786 --> 00:08:51.069
This dead man is the traitor Robert Mackenzie.

00:08:51.129 --> 00:08:52.700
Mackenzie?

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.831
Why are you giving shelter to traitors?

00:08:54.891 --> 00:08:57.383
No, no, I'm not giving them shelter.

00:08:57.443 --> 00:08:58.133
I promise.

00:08:58.173 --> 00:09:01.395
People who shelter traitors are also traitors.

00:09:01.455 --> 00:09:03.356
But I didn't shelter them.

00:09:03.416 --> 00:09:04.717
I wouldn't let them in.

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:08.097
Guards, take him away.

00:09:08.157 --> 00:09:10.818
I have nothing wrong!

00:09:10.878 --> 00:09:12.660
What is the name of this cottage?

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.013
It is known as McPherson's Farm.

00:09:15.073 --> 00:09:30.411
Burn it to the ground.

00:09:30.472 --> 00:09:52.454
Scotland 2005 Excuse me.

00:09:52.514 --> 00:09:53.774
Yes?

00:09:53.834 --> 00:09:57.367
Are you Walter McPherson?

00:09:57.427 --> 00:09:58.858
Yes, I am.

00:09:58.918 --> 00:09:59.708
Oh!

00:09:59.768 --> 00:10:01.550
How amazing!

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:02.170
Sorry?

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:04.732
Well, I've just finished reading your book.

00:10:04.792 --> 00:10:05.753
Which one?

00:10:05.813 --> 00:10:07.344
I've written quite a few.

00:10:07.404 --> 00:10:09.665
The Ghosts of Eddington Castle.

00:10:09.725 --> 00:10:11.196
It's brilliant!

00:10:11.256 --> 00:10:12.289
Thank you.

00:10:12.349 --> 00:10:15.122
My name's Jane Duncan, by the way.

00:10:15.182 --> 00:10:16.924
Please to meet you, Miss.

00:10:16.984 --> 00:10:18.464
Miss Duncan.

00:10:18.524 --> 00:10:19.845
Call me, Jane.

00:10:19.905 --> 00:10:21.986
Please to meet you, Jane.

00:10:22.046 --> 00:10:23.828
Tell me.

00:10:23.888 --> 00:10:26.559
Are you on your way to Eddington now?

00:10:26.619 --> 00:10:28.920
Yes, I am as a matter of fact.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.211
Really?

00:10:30.271 --> 00:10:32.852
I'm actually from Eddington.

00:10:32.912 --> 00:10:33.953
Are you?

00:10:34.013 --> 00:10:35.454
Do you live there?

00:10:35.514 --> 00:10:37.855
No, I live in Eddington.

00:10:37.915 --> 00:10:40.116
I'm coming home to see my parents.

00:10:40.176 --> 00:10:41.448
I see.

00:10:41.507 --> 00:10:44.860
Walter, are you in English, aren't you?

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:46.392
Oh, you noticed.

00:10:46.452 --> 00:10:48.094
I certainly did.

00:10:48.154 --> 00:10:50.025
I'm surprised.

00:10:50.085 --> 00:10:51.116
Surprised?

00:10:51.176 --> 00:10:52.036
Why?

00:10:52.096 --> 00:10:57.142
I thought that the ghosts of Eddington Castle was written by someone from the area.

00:10:57.202 --> 00:11:02.066
Well, for a stop, my ancestors are from the area around Eddington.

00:11:02.126 --> 00:11:03.276
Right!

00:11:03.336 --> 00:11:06.470
MacPherson is a very common name in the area.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:09.540
And secondly, I own a house in Eddington.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.038
Do you know?

00:11:11.098 --> 00:11:12.559
Which one?

00:11:12.619 --> 00:11:15.540
McPherson's farmhouse.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:20.132
You own McPherson's farmhouse?

00:11:20.192 --> 00:11:20.852
Yes.

00:11:20.912 --> 00:11:24.683
Well, I inherited it from my cousin, Alistair.

00:11:24.743 --> 00:11:25.784
Oh.

00:11:25.844 --> 00:11:27.234
Was he?

00:11:27.294 --> 00:11:29.275
Was he the man who died there?

00:11:29.335 --> 00:11:30.015
Yes.

00:11:30.075 --> 00:11:31.756
Alistair McPherson?

00:11:31.816 --> 00:11:33.326
Yes, I see.

00:11:33.346 --> 00:11:36.307
How long?

00:11:36.367 --> 00:11:38.092
It was five years ago.

00:11:38.152 --> 00:11:40.628
And is it true?

00:11:40.688 --> 00:11:41.688
What?

00:11:41.748 --> 00:11:42.949
Is what true?

00:11:43.009 --> 00:11:47.720
Is it true that he only spent one night at the house before he died?

00:11:47.781 --> 00:11:49.111
Yes, it is.

00:11:49.171 --> 00:11:52.692
He died of a heart attack on his first night in the house.

00:11:52.752 --> 00:11:54.193
Very strange.

00:11:54.253 --> 00:11:55.203
I see.

00:11:55.223 --> 00:11:59.225
You know people in the village think...

00:11:59.285 --> 00:12:00.326
I know.

00:12:00.386 --> 00:12:03.151
I know they think that the farmhouse is haunted.

00:12:03.211 --> 00:12:03.962
Yes.

00:12:04.022 --> 00:12:05.776
Well, I'm not sure.

00:12:05.836 --> 00:12:08.460
For the start, it isn't the original farmhouse.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.474
The original farmhouse burnt down.

00:12:10.534 --> 00:12:12.315
This one is only 200 years old.

00:12:12.375 --> 00:12:16.426
I know, but it's built on exactly the same spot.

00:12:16.486 --> 00:12:17.056
Really?

00:12:17.116 --> 00:12:17.958
Really?

00:12:18.018 --> 00:12:20.400
And take my work for it, Walter.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:25.694
People in Eddington believe that the farmhouse and the castle are haunted.

00:12:25.754 --> 00:12:28.676
So many strange things have happened there.

00:12:28.736 --> 00:12:31.498
I know, I spent months researching that book.

00:12:31.558 --> 00:12:35.852
I know all about the horses galloping across the hills near the castle late at night.

00:12:35.912 --> 00:12:38.754
Well, a lot of people have heard them.

00:12:38.815 --> 00:12:39.743
Have you?

00:12:39.803 --> 00:12:41.681
Well, no.

00:12:41.721 --> 00:12:47.623
You see, you actually ask anyone if they've seen these horses and they say, no.

00:12:47.683 --> 00:12:50.074
But my uncle McPavage has.

00:12:50.134 --> 00:12:55.725
So, I asked if I could meet these uncles and grandfathers and of course they were all dead.

00:12:55.785 --> 00:12:56.645
Well...

00:12:56.705 --> 00:12:58.376
Anyway, I don't care.

00:12:58.436 --> 00:13:01.386
It's my house and I'm going to live there.

00:13:01.446 --> 00:13:05.598
You're going to live at McPherson's farmhouse.

00:13:05.658 --> 00:13:06.455
Yes.

00:13:06.515 --> 00:13:08.273
What, at the weekends?

00:13:08.333 --> 00:13:09.814
No, all the time.

00:13:09.873 --> 00:13:11.934
Goodness!

00:13:11.994 --> 00:13:15.046
Well, you feel safe there.

00:13:15.106 --> 00:13:16.207
Safe?

00:13:16.267 --> 00:13:20.019
Jane, I've lived in London for the last 20 years.

00:13:20.079 --> 00:13:25.952
In my street, every day I see tramps, drug dealers, hooligans, football fans.

00:13:26.012 --> 00:13:27.413
I've had enough.

00:13:27.473 --> 00:13:29.224
You've had enough of London?

00:13:29.284 --> 00:13:30.184
Absolutely.

00:13:30.244 --> 00:13:31.876
It's dirty and expensive.

00:13:31.936 --> 00:13:33.686
And I'm a writer, not a banker.

00:13:33.746 --> 00:13:35.588
So I can't afford to live there anymore.

00:13:35.647 --> 00:13:36.801
I see.

00:13:36.861 --> 00:13:38.515
And I'm too old for it.

00:13:38.575 --> 00:13:40.826
Everyone seems to be under 30.

00:13:40.886 --> 00:13:42.798
How old are you?

00:13:42.858 --> 00:13:44.360
31.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:46.371
Goodness.

00:13:46.431 --> 00:13:47.702
I'm 31.

00:13:47.762 --> 00:13:49.623
I was joking, Jane.

00:13:49.683 --> 00:13:51.745
I'm a little bit older than 31.

00:13:51.805 --> 00:13:54.615
Anyway, I decided it was time for a change.

00:13:54.675 --> 00:14:00.306
But you want to live in McPherson's farmhouse?

00:14:00.366 --> 00:14:03.399
No one has lived there for ages.

00:14:03.459 --> 00:14:04.700
I mean, apart from...

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.842
Ah, apart from Alistair, I know.

00:14:06.902 --> 00:14:08.653
But I am going to live there.

00:14:08.713 --> 00:14:13.026
In fact, I moved all my books on a lot of my furniture up there last month.

00:14:13.086 --> 00:14:16.248
And a nice lady from the village has cleaned the place up for me.

00:14:16.308 --> 00:14:17.910
She's done a wonderful job.

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:19.491
I'm sure she has.

00:14:19.551 --> 00:14:23.627
Eddington people are very hard-working.

00:14:23.688 --> 00:14:26.882
Tell me something Walter.

00:14:26.942 --> 00:14:28.173
What?

00:14:28.233 --> 00:14:32.124
Have you ever spent the night at the farmhouse?

00:14:32.184 --> 00:14:34.024
Not yet, no.

00:14:34.084 --> 00:14:37.254
Tonight will be the first night.

00:14:37.314 --> 00:14:43.796
Melrose, next station Melrose, change here from a govern, Haven and Eddington.

00:14:43.856 --> 00:14:45.607
We have to change here.

00:14:45.667 --> 00:14:51.853
Okay.

00:14:51.914 --> 00:14:59.230
Walter.

00:14:59.291 --> 00:15:00.962
What?

00:15:01.022 --> 00:15:01.962
Week out.

00:15:02.022 --> 00:15:02.672
Why?

00:15:02.732 --> 00:15:03.863
We've arrived.

00:15:03.923 --> 00:15:04.853
Where are we?

00:15:04.913 --> 00:15:06.054
In Eddington.

00:15:06.114 --> 00:15:09.535
Oh, right.

00:15:09.595 --> 00:15:13.367
How are you going to get to the farmhouse?

00:15:13.427 --> 00:15:14.287
I don't know.

00:15:14.307 --> 00:15:16.318
Like taxi, I suppose.

00:15:16.378 --> 00:15:17.618
Taxi?

00:15:17.678 --> 00:15:19.189
This time of night.

00:15:19.249 --> 00:15:21.190
No chance.

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:23.260
Well, I'll walk.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:24.131
Walk?

00:15:24.191 --> 00:15:25.321
Don't be silly.

00:15:25.381 --> 00:15:27.962
It's about three miles outside the village.

00:15:28.022 --> 00:15:31.153
At that case, I don't know what I'll do.

00:15:31.213 --> 00:15:35.624
Look, my father will be waiting for me outside the station.

00:15:35.684 --> 00:15:44.562
He can give you a lift.

00:15:44.623 --> 00:15:54.801
It's awfully nice of you to give me a lift, Mr. Duncan.

00:15:54.861 --> 00:15:57.121
Think nothing of it, Mr. McPherson.

00:15:57.181 --> 00:16:01.752
Walter thought you would be able to get a taxi at the station further.

00:16:01.812 --> 00:16:07.564
Well, there is a taxi in the village, but the driver stops work at six o'clock.

00:16:07.624 --> 00:16:10.074
I don't know how I would have done without you.

00:16:10.134 --> 00:16:13.155
In London, I go everywhere by bus or taxi.

00:16:13.215 --> 00:16:14.435
I don't have a car.

00:16:14.495 --> 00:16:16.436
Waste of time and money.

00:16:16.496 --> 00:16:18.186
What did you see?

00:16:18.246 --> 00:16:21.037
It's a waste of time and money, owning a car.

00:16:21.097 --> 00:16:22.308
Really?

00:16:22.368 --> 00:16:24.560
Well, not up here, of course.

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:27.152
I'm sure you need a car all the time up here.

00:16:27.212 --> 00:16:28.242
Yes.

00:16:28.302 --> 00:16:29.884
I'm sure we do.

00:16:29.944 --> 00:16:38.420
We're coming to the farmhouse now.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:45.556
Goodness.

00:16:45.616 --> 00:16:47.014
Stock out here, isn't it?

00:16:47.074 --> 00:16:48.293
Yes, it is.

00:16:48.353 --> 00:16:49.634
Very dark.

00:16:49.694 --> 00:16:55.888
I say, Mr. Duncan, could you point your headlights at the front door so I can see what I'm doing?

00:16:55.948 --> 00:17:02.032
Just a minute.

00:17:02.092 --> 00:17:07.706
That's marvellous.

00:17:07.746 --> 00:17:11.098
Thank you.

00:17:11.158 --> 00:17:15.771
Well, here we are.

00:17:15.831 --> 00:17:17.262
Home, sweet home.

00:17:17.322 --> 00:17:19.693
Do you want to come in and have a look around?

00:17:19.753 --> 00:17:20.574
Eh...

00:17:20.634 --> 00:17:21.394
Come on.

00:17:21.454 --> 00:17:22.464
Don't be shy.

00:17:22.524 --> 00:17:23.474
Jean!

00:17:23.534 --> 00:17:25.014
Don't go in there!

00:17:25.074 --> 00:17:26.385
Father!

00:17:26.445 --> 00:17:27.695
I mean it.

00:17:27.755 --> 00:17:33.136
I don't mind driving Mr. McPherson here, but I don't want you to go into the house.

00:17:33.196 --> 00:17:34.916
Sorry, Mr. McPherson.

00:17:34.976 --> 00:17:36.566
It's nothing personal.

00:17:36.626 --> 00:17:38.327
No, no, I understand.

00:17:38.387 --> 00:17:39.547
You country types?

00:17:39.607 --> 00:17:41.147
I beg your pardon?

00:17:41.207 --> 00:17:42.377
Sorry, I mean...

00:17:42.437 --> 00:17:43.188
Walter.

00:17:43.248 --> 00:17:45.872
Dad and I are going home now.

00:17:45.933 --> 00:17:47.978
Here's my phone number.

00:17:48.038 --> 00:17:51.589
If you need anything, just give me a call.

00:17:51.649 --> 00:17:53.840
Well, thank you.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:55.690
Do you have a phone here?

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:57.461
No, not yet.

00:17:57.521 --> 00:18:00.002
But I've got a mobile here.

00:18:00.062 --> 00:18:01.623
The number's on this card.

00:18:01.683 --> 00:18:02.513
OK.

00:18:02.573 --> 00:18:05.534
I'll call you later to make sure everything is all right.

00:18:05.595 --> 00:18:08.086
Goodbye.

00:18:08.146 --> 00:18:10.716
Thank you, Jane.

00:18:10.776 --> 00:18:12.287
Thanks for everything.

00:18:12.347 --> 00:18:13.288
Jane!

00:18:13.348 --> 00:18:24.034
Coming!

00:18:24.094 --> 00:18:34.849
Good God.

00:18:34.909 --> 00:18:36.639
It's quiet around here.

00:18:36.699 --> 00:18:40.580
And it's so dark.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:47.692
What on earth is that?

00:18:47.752 --> 00:18:51.552
Pull yourself together, Walter.

00:18:51.612 --> 00:18:54.732
It's time to have a look at your new home.

00:18:54.792 --> 00:18:58.652
Now where the hell is the light switch?

00:18:58.712 --> 00:19:01.013
Don't blast.

00:19:01.073 --> 00:19:02.984
The lights aren't working.

00:19:03.044 --> 00:19:06.504
Oh well, I'm up to sort that out in the morning.

00:19:06.564 --> 00:19:15.577
So, the bedroom's in here, I think.

00:19:15.638 --> 00:19:18.739
Jesus Christ, it's a cat.

00:19:18.799 --> 00:19:20.779
How the hell did you get in here?

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:26.115
Well, you're going out.

00:19:26.175 --> 00:19:31.050
Oh my God.

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:32.631
There's that noise again.

00:19:32.691 --> 00:19:33.491
There we are!

00:19:33.551 --> 00:19:34.332
Fire!

00:19:34.392 --> 00:19:36.282
Altar, pull yourself together.

00:19:36.342 --> 00:19:40.703
There are no ghosts at Eddington Castle.

00:19:40.764 --> 00:19:43.985
Time for bed.

00:19:44.045 --> 00:19:46.786
I wish to God there was some whiskey somewhere.

00:19:46.846 --> 00:19:51.678
What?

00:19:51.738 --> 00:19:53.678
Where am I?

00:19:53.739 --> 00:19:55.209
Hello?

00:19:55.269 --> 00:19:56.229
Water?

00:19:56.289 --> 00:19:57.219
Who's that?

00:19:57.279 --> 00:19:58.330
It's Jane.

00:19:58.390 --> 00:19:59.820
Jane Duncan.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.372
Jane?

00:20:01.432 --> 00:20:03.682
Oh Jane, hello.

00:20:03.742 --> 00:20:04.883
What time is it?

00:20:04.943 --> 00:20:06.554
It's half past ten.

00:20:06.614 --> 00:20:08.284
Sorry, did I wake you up?

00:20:08.344 --> 00:20:10.905
No, no, I was just...

00:20:10.966 --> 00:20:13.447
Well, yes, you did actually.

00:20:13.507 --> 00:20:15.668
I'm so sorry Walter.

00:20:15.728 --> 00:20:17.909
I should have waited until tomorrow.

00:20:17.969 --> 00:20:20.866
I just wanted to see if everything was alright.

00:20:20.926 --> 00:20:23.444
Yes, everything's fine.

00:20:23.504 --> 00:20:27.916
There's no electricity and no whiskey, but apart from that, no problems at all.

00:20:27.976 --> 00:20:30.508
Well, I'm very pleased to hear it.

00:20:30.568 --> 00:20:34.049
I was wondering what your plans were for tomorrow.

00:20:34.109 --> 00:20:36.240
Well, I...

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:38.502
God, what was that?

00:20:38.562 --> 00:20:39.852
What?

00:20:39.912 --> 00:20:41.633
What is it, Walter?

00:20:41.693 --> 00:20:43.504
Someone's knocking on the door.

00:20:43.564 --> 00:20:44.874
Fit awake in the dead.

00:20:44.934 --> 00:20:46.185
Can't you hear it?

00:20:46.245 --> 00:20:47.586
No, Walter.

00:20:47.646 --> 00:20:50.861
I can't hear anything at all.

00:20:50.921 --> 00:20:53.636
I store mighty.

00:20:53.696 --> 00:20:54.937
Did you hear that?

00:20:54.997 --> 00:20:55.928
No.

00:20:55.988 --> 00:20:57.588
What's going on?

00:20:57.648 --> 00:21:00.960
There's a woman at the door, shouting ahead of.

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:02.910
I'm going to tell her to get lost.

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:04.902
Walter, don't.

00:21:04.962 --> 00:21:07.182
Don't open the door.

00:21:07.242 --> 00:21:08.473
Hold on a second, Jane.

00:21:08.533 --> 00:21:09.723
I'll sort it out.

00:21:09.784 --> 00:21:11.554
Walter, stop it.

00:21:11.614 --> 00:21:13.525
Don't open the door.

00:21:13.585 --> 00:21:15.566
Open the door.

00:21:15.626 --> 00:21:18.277
I've just about had enough.

00:21:18.337 --> 00:21:20.978
Open the door.

00:21:21.038 --> 00:21:22.367
Who's there?

00:21:22.427 --> 00:21:24.047
Open the door, I tell you!

00:21:24.107 --> 00:21:25.318
But who are you?

00:21:25.378 --> 00:21:26.618
Open the door!

00:21:26.638 --> 00:21:29.048
They're going to kill us!

00:21:29.108 --> 00:21:31.129
Who are you?

00:21:31.189 --> 00:21:32.979
My God!

00:21:33.039 --> 00:21:34.299
What's happened to this man?

00:21:34.359 --> 00:21:35.970
The English are after us!

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:37.850
The English, what are you talking about?

00:21:37.910 --> 00:21:39.300
Let us in!

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:39.600
No!

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:41.710
Tell me who you are!

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:43.901
What the hell?

00:21:43.961 --> 00:21:46.952
Who are all these people?

00:21:47.012 --> 00:21:51.374
Oh my God!

00:21:51.434 --> 00:21:56.827
will regret this moment until your dying day.

00:21:56.887 --> 00:22:04.530
In the name of Scotland, I put a curse on your family for all time!

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:06.020
Fire!

00:22:06.080 --> 00:22:11.173
Oh my god!

00:22:11.232 --> 00:22:14.926
It's all true.

00:22:14.986 --> 00:22:18.352
Walter!

00:22:18.412 --> 00:22:20.210
What's happened?

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:23.360
Walter!

00:22:23.420 --> 00:22:25.843
Hello?

00:22:25.903 --> 00:22:27.274
Is that the police?

00:22:27.334 --> 00:22:28.614
Yes, it is.

00:22:28.674 --> 00:22:32.545
My name is Jane Duncan, and I'm calling from Eddington.

00:22:32.605 --> 00:22:33.795
Eddington?

00:22:33.855 --> 00:22:36.656
Now, that's near Haber, am I right?

00:22:36.716 --> 00:22:37.466
Yes!

00:22:37.526 --> 00:22:39.236
You have to send someone!

00:22:39.296 --> 00:22:41.167
Something terrible has happened!

00:22:41.227 --> 00:22:42.007
Really?

00:22:42.067 --> 00:22:43.567
Now, what would that be?

00:22:43.587 --> 00:22:46.688
I think someone may have been murdered.

00:22:46.748 --> 00:22:47.438
Murdered?

00:22:47.498 --> 00:22:48.188
Where?

00:22:48.248 --> 00:22:50.189
McPherson's farmhouse.

00:22:50.249 --> 00:22:55.780
Please get police and an ambulance there as fast as you can!

00:22:55.840 --> 00:22:57.792
Father?

00:22:57.852 --> 00:22:58.952
What is it, Jane?

00:22:59.012 --> 00:23:01.443
We have to go back to the farmhouse right away.

00:23:01.503 --> 00:23:02.164
Why?

00:23:02.224 --> 00:23:03.064
What's happened?

00:23:03.124 --> 00:23:07.877
Walter is in terrible trouble.

00:23:07.937 --> 00:23:13.730
Oh my God, Walter's at the door.

00:23:13.790 --> 00:23:16.462
Walter, are you all right?

00:23:16.522 --> 00:23:17.892
Please, no more.

00:23:17.952 --> 00:23:19.103
He's alive.

00:23:19.163 --> 00:23:20.944
Father, here's my phone.

00:23:21.004 --> 00:23:22.335
Call the police again.

00:23:22.395 --> 00:23:23.533
Hi.

00:23:23.593 --> 00:23:26.673
Walter, can you hear me?

00:23:26.733 --> 00:23:27.444
Yes.

00:23:27.504 --> 00:23:29.204
What happened?

00:23:29.264 --> 00:23:31.146
A man and a woman.

00:23:31.206 --> 00:23:32.618
They were trying to get in.

00:23:32.678 --> 00:23:33.828
A man and a woman?

00:23:33.848 --> 00:23:34.458
Yes.

00:23:34.518 --> 00:23:36.060
What did they look like?

00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:36.820
What?

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:38.852
I don't know.

00:23:38.912 --> 00:23:40.464
God.

00:23:40.524 --> 00:23:41.644
Did it hit me?

00:23:41.704 --> 00:23:43.306
Did what hit you, Walter?

00:23:43.366 --> 00:23:44.106
The arrow.

00:23:44.166 --> 00:23:45.137
The arrow?

00:23:45.197 --> 00:23:46.128
Did it hit me?

00:23:46.188 --> 00:23:47.028
No, Walter.

00:23:47.088 --> 00:23:48.029
It didn't hit you.

00:23:48.089 --> 00:23:49.708
Thank God for that.

00:23:49.768 --> 00:23:50.866
Jean.

00:23:50.926 --> 00:23:51.737
What, Father?

00:23:51.797 --> 00:23:53.469
The ambulance is on its way.

00:23:53.529 --> 00:23:53.989
Good.

00:23:54.049 --> 00:23:54.850
Thank you.

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:56.011
Is he all right?

00:23:56.071 --> 00:23:58.854
Well, he's alive, but he isn't all right.

00:23:58.914 --> 00:24:01.875
I think he's had a heart attack or something.

00:24:01.936 --> 00:24:03.468
And?

00:24:03.528 --> 00:24:14.945
And I think he's seen the ghosts of Elizabeth and Robert Mackenzie.

00:24:15.005 --> 00:24:24.641
My name is Detective Sergeant Jackson, and you are...

00:24:24.701 --> 00:24:28.244
My name's Jane Duncan, and this is my father, Donald.

00:24:28.304 --> 00:24:28.945
Hello.

00:24:29.005 --> 00:24:29.696
Hello.

00:24:29.756 --> 00:24:31.257
Sorry to keep you both waiting.

00:24:31.317 --> 00:24:32.238
That's alright.

00:24:32.298 --> 00:24:35.861
We just wanted to make sure that the gentleman was on his way to hospital.

00:24:35.921 --> 00:24:37.092
I understand.

00:24:37.152 --> 00:24:38.904
Is he going to be alright?

00:24:38.964 --> 00:24:40.045
I don't know.

00:24:40.105 --> 00:24:41.486
He's had a heart attack.

00:24:41.546 --> 00:24:43.198
The medics did what they could.

00:24:43.258 --> 00:24:44.609
We'll have to wait and see.

00:24:44.669 --> 00:24:45.585
Okay.

00:24:45.645 --> 00:24:49.672
Now, if you don't mind, I need to ask you one or two questions.

00:24:49.732 --> 00:24:51.012
I know it's a bit late.

00:24:51.072 --> 00:24:51.813
That's all right.

00:24:51.873 --> 00:24:52.933
It's not a problem.

00:24:52.993 --> 00:24:53.523
Right.

00:24:53.583 --> 00:24:58.115
Well, first of all, I understand that you found the gentleman.

00:24:58.175 --> 00:24:58.846
Yes.

00:24:58.906 --> 00:25:00.616
Where was he when you found him?

00:25:00.676 --> 00:25:02.607
He was lying in the doorway.

00:25:02.667 --> 00:25:05.488
And did he tell you what had happened to him?

00:25:05.548 --> 00:25:11.323
Not exactly, but I think he saw the ghosts of Eddington Castle.

00:25:11.383 --> 00:25:13.736
He saw what?

00:25:13.797 --> 00:25:16.198
He saw two ghosts.

00:25:16.258 --> 00:25:18.930
I can't write that in my report.

00:25:18.990 --> 00:25:22.762
Mr. Jackson, you aren't from round here, are you?

00:25:22.822 --> 00:25:24.613
No, I'm from Glasgow.

00:25:24.673 --> 00:25:27.975
Did you see a ruined castle when you drove here?

00:25:28.035 --> 00:25:29.596
No, it's dark.

00:25:29.616 --> 00:25:30.767
I didn't see anything.

00:25:30.827 --> 00:25:34.640
Well, you drove past Eddington Castle.

00:25:34.700 --> 00:25:38.820
Most people around here would tell you that there are ghosts there.

00:25:38.880 --> 00:25:40.538
Ghosts, eh?

00:25:40.598 --> 00:25:41.989
Anybody famous?

00:25:42.049 --> 00:25:45.470
Detective, this is no laughing matter.

00:25:45.530 --> 00:25:48.571
The ghosts are two Scottish freedom fighters.

00:25:48.631 --> 00:25:51.022
Elizabeth and Robert Mackenzie.

00:25:51.082 --> 00:25:54.393
They fought against the English in the 17th century.

00:25:54.453 --> 00:25:57.194
They were killed somewhere in these fields.

00:25:57.254 --> 00:26:01.006
People have seen the ghosts of the English soldiers who killed them as well.

00:26:01.066 --> 00:26:02.046
I see.

00:26:02.106 --> 00:26:05.338
Well, let's talk about what happened this evening.

00:26:05.398 --> 00:26:10.622
By the way, what is your relationship with the gentleman?

00:26:10.682 --> 00:26:13.213
I met him on the train from Edinburgh this evening.

00:26:13.273 --> 00:26:15.724
We gave him a lift to the farmhouse.

00:26:15.784 --> 00:26:16.634
I see.

00:26:16.694 --> 00:26:19.256
So you were here when he had the heart attack?

00:26:19.316 --> 00:26:19.896
No.

00:26:19.956 --> 00:26:25.008
We brought Mr McPherson here, but my father didn't want to go into the house.

00:26:25.068 --> 00:26:25.929
Really?

00:26:25.989 --> 00:26:27.039
Why not?

00:26:27.100 --> 00:26:30.442
Everyone in Eddington is frightened of this house.

00:26:30.502 --> 00:26:33.520
No one has lived here for five years.

00:26:33.580 --> 00:26:37.953
Walter, Mr. McPherson, owns the cottage now.

00:26:38.013 --> 00:26:41.285
But tonight was the first night he spent here.

00:26:41.345 --> 00:26:43.784
He tried to spend here.

00:26:43.844 --> 00:26:44.734
Right.

00:26:44.794 --> 00:26:49.349
And the last person who lived here died the first night he was here.

00:26:49.409 --> 00:26:51.741
So, let me get this straight.

00:26:51.801 --> 00:26:57.486
Mr. McPherson is the owner of the cottage, but he's never spent any time here.

00:26:57.546 --> 00:26:58.457
That's right.

00:26:58.517 --> 00:27:03.511
So, you brought Mr. McPherson to the house and then you went home.

00:27:03.572 --> 00:27:04.322
Yes.

00:27:04.382 --> 00:27:06.904
So, why did you come back to the cottage?

00:27:06.964 --> 00:27:08.780
I came because...

00:27:08.840 --> 00:27:09.784
Yes.

00:27:09.844 --> 00:27:13.588
Well, I called Walter to see if he was all right.

00:27:13.648 --> 00:27:14.788
Yes.

00:27:14.848 --> 00:27:18.041
And something happened while we were on the phone.

00:27:18.101 --> 00:27:20.573
He said there was someone at the door.

00:27:20.633 --> 00:27:23.745
He opened the door and started talking to someone.

00:27:23.805 --> 00:27:25.827
Did you hear who he was talking to?

00:27:25.887 --> 00:27:26.568
No.

00:27:26.628 --> 00:27:28.960
I could only hear Walter's voice.

00:27:29.020 --> 00:27:30.240
What did he see?

00:27:30.300 --> 00:27:32.602
He said, he said...

00:27:32.663 --> 00:27:34.064
Who are you?

00:27:34.124 --> 00:27:35.525
My God!

00:27:35.585 --> 00:27:37.106
What's happened to this matter?

00:27:37.166 --> 00:27:37.846
English?

00:27:37.906 --> 00:27:39.037
What are you talking about?

00:27:39.057 --> 00:27:39.698
No!

00:27:39.758 --> 00:27:41.489
Tell me who you are!

00:27:41.549 --> 00:27:42.940
The hell!

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:44.481
Who are all these people?

00:27:44.541 --> 00:27:45.862
Oh my God!

00:27:45.922 --> 00:27:47.423
It's all true!

00:27:47.483 --> 00:27:48.744
It's all true!

00:27:48.804 --> 00:27:50.005
It's all true!

00:27:50.065 --> 00:27:52.276
It's all true!

00:27:52.336 --> 00:27:55.040
Mr. McPherson?

00:27:55.100 --> 00:27:57.362
Mr. McPherson.

00:27:57.422 --> 00:27:59.062
What?

00:27:59.122 --> 00:28:01.024
Oh, nurse.

00:28:01.084 --> 00:28:02.575
What time is it?

00:28:02.635 --> 00:28:04.066
It's half past nine.

00:28:04.126 --> 00:28:06.337
Mr. McPherson and you have a visitor.

00:28:06.397 --> 00:28:08.288
Good morning, Walter.

00:28:08.348 --> 00:28:11.049
Jane, how good to see you.

00:28:11.110 --> 00:28:12.930
Good to see you too, Walter.

00:28:12.990 --> 00:28:14.241
You look great.

00:28:14.301 --> 00:28:16.892
Yes, and they're letting me out today.

00:28:16.952 --> 00:28:18.020
I know.

00:28:18.080 --> 00:28:21.750
Walter, I'm sorry I didn't come to see you earlier.

00:28:21.810 --> 00:28:25.803
I had to go back to Edinburgh, but I came back as soon as I could.

00:28:25.863 --> 00:28:28.374
It's so good to see you, Jane.

00:28:28.434 --> 00:28:31.247
You know you saved my life, don't you?

00:28:31.307 --> 00:28:33.829
Oh, Walter, it was nothing.

00:28:33.849 --> 00:28:36.130
No, you're wrong.

00:28:36.191 --> 00:28:41.354
The doctors told me, if you hadn't come to the house, I would have died.

00:28:41.414 --> 00:28:44.886
Well, only too glad to help.

00:28:44.946 --> 00:28:47.398
It was terrifying, you know?

00:28:47.458 --> 00:28:49.392
I can imagine.

00:28:49.452 --> 00:28:54.176
This woman, she looked as if she was going to kill me.

00:28:54.236 --> 00:28:55.456
Yes.

00:28:55.516 --> 00:28:57.938
And do you know what the man said?

00:28:57.998 --> 00:29:07.914
He said, in the name of Scotland, I put a curse on your family for all time.

00:29:07.974 --> 00:29:09.804
A curse?

00:29:09.865 --> 00:29:11.104
Yes.

00:29:11.164 --> 00:29:17.845
Your family is cursed because the man in the farmhouse didn't let Robert and Elizabeth into the house.

00:29:17.905 --> 00:29:20.175
Well, it seems that way.

00:29:20.236 --> 00:29:25.077
Walter, this may seem like a ridiculous question, but...

00:29:25.137 --> 00:29:26.218
Go on.

00:29:26.278 --> 00:29:28.868
Are you going to go back to the farmhouse?

00:29:28.928 --> 00:29:29.808
No way.

00:29:29.868 --> 00:29:30.959
Are you sure?

00:29:31.019 --> 00:29:32.329
Absolutely.

00:29:32.389 --> 00:29:38.226
I'm going to put it on the market, and if no one wants to buy it, I'm going to set fire to it.

00:29:38.286 --> 00:29:40.781
I don't think you should do that.

00:29:40.841 --> 00:29:44.683
I think there's something we can do to solve the problem.

00:29:44.743 --> 00:29:45.534
We?

00:29:45.594 --> 00:29:47.054
Yes, we.

00:29:47.114 --> 00:29:48.656
I'll help you.

00:29:48.716 --> 00:29:55.019
Walter, you and I are going to spend the night at the farmhouse tonight.

00:29:55.079 --> 00:29:56.160
What?

00:29:56.220 --> 00:30:01.370
No way.

00:30:01.430 --> 00:30:07.362
Thank you very much, Mr. Pearson.

00:30:07.422 --> 00:30:08.483
Ah, you're welcome.

00:30:08.543 --> 00:30:09.833
How much is that?

00:30:09.893 --> 00:30:11.054
Oh, nothing, Jean.

00:30:11.114 --> 00:30:12.625
This trip is on the house.

00:30:12.685 --> 00:30:18.738
Oh, thank you.

00:30:18.798 --> 00:30:25.572
I can't believe that I'm doing this.

00:30:25.632 --> 00:30:27.643
Walter, trust me.

00:30:27.703 --> 00:30:32.644
We're doing the right thing.

00:30:32.704 --> 00:30:39.436
Well, are you going to come in this time?

00:30:39.497 --> 00:30:40.948
Of course.

00:30:41.008 --> 00:30:42.938
You won't be able to see anything.

00:30:42.999 --> 00:30:44.180
Yes, I will.

00:30:44.240 --> 00:30:45.680
I brought these.

00:30:45.740 --> 00:30:47.032
Candles.

00:30:47.092 --> 00:30:51.034
Good idea.

00:30:51.094 --> 00:30:57.958
Oh, Walter, it's absolutely beautiful.

00:30:58.019 --> 00:30:59.269
Yes.

00:30:59.330 --> 00:31:00.350
You're right.

00:31:00.410 --> 00:31:01.490
I'd forgotten.

00:31:01.550 --> 00:31:04.840
By the way, what does your father think about you being here?

00:31:04.900 --> 00:31:05.848
He doesn't know.

00:31:05.868 --> 00:31:07.229
He doesn't know.

00:31:07.289 --> 00:31:07.830
No.

00:31:07.890 --> 00:31:09.822
He thinks I'm in Edinburgh.

00:31:09.882 --> 00:31:12.103
I haven't told him that I came back.

00:31:12.163 --> 00:31:14.505
Jane, this is crazy.

00:31:14.565 --> 00:31:16.337
Walter, relax.

00:31:16.397 --> 00:31:21.542
We just have to spend the night here and then everything will be fine.

00:31:21.602 --> 00:31:23.693
You know there isn't any electricity.

00:31:23.753 --> 00:31:24.424
Yes.

00:31:24.484 --> 00:31:26.946
So I can't even make you a cup of tea.

00:31:27.006 --> 00:31:29.009
But I do have this.

00:31:29.069 --> 00:31:30.671
A bottle of whiskey.

00:31:30.731 --> 00:31:32.352
Do you want some?

00:31:32.372 --> 00:31:32.712
No.

00:31:32.772 --> 00:31:34.762
And you mustn't have any either.

00:31:34.822 --> 00:31:37.623
You had a heart attack less than a week ago.

00:31:37.683 --> 00:31:38.404
I know.

00:31:38.464 --> 00:31:41.144
That's why I want some whiskey.

00:31:41.204 --> 00:31:44.145
So, what do we do now?

00:31:44.205 --> 00:31:46.036
We wait.

00:31:46.096 --> 00:31:50.427
Jane, if you want to sleep, you can have my room.

00:31:50.487 --> 00:31:52.198
I can sleep here in the kitchen.

00:31:52.258 --> 00:31:56.270
Walter, I don't need to...

00:31:56.330 --> 00:31:59.762
Can you hear that?

00:31:59.822 --> 00:32:00.944
Yes.

00:32:01.004 --> 00:32:02.664
Oh, God.

00:32:02.724 --> 00:32:05.006
Can we call the police or something?

00:32:05.066 --> 00:32:07.017
We don't need the police.

00:32:07.077 --> 00:32:08.388
Let me go to the window.

00:32:08.448 --> 00:32:09.138
No!

00:32:09.198 --> 00:32:15.692
Walter, just stay where you are.

00:32:15.752 --> 00:32:20.945
Robert, let me help you.

00:32:21.006 --> 00:32:23.768
Lean against the wall.

00:32:23.828 --> 00:32:25.918
Go, Princess!

00:32:25.978 --> 00:32:26.689
Go!

00:32:26.749 --> 00:32:31.790
Run into the forest!

00:32:31.850 --> 00:32:35.780
Jane.

00:32:35.840 --> 00:32:37.042
Wait.

00:32:37.102 --> 00:32:40.583
Open the door.

00:32:40.643 --> 00:32:43.435
Don't move, Walter.

00:32:43.495 --> 00:32:45.156
Let me deal with this.

00:32:45.216 --> 00:32:47.818
Jane, what are you doing?

00:32:47.878 --> 00:32:50.360
I'm going to open the door.

00:32:50.420 --> 00:32:51.560
Jane, don't.

00:32:51.620 --> 00:32:52.451
I'll kill you.

00:32:52.511 --> 00:32:54.452
Walter, trust me.

00:32:54.472 --> 00:32:58.284
Open the door.

00:32:58.345 --> 00:33:00.516
Welcome.

00:33:00.576 --> 00:33:02.154
Come in.

00:33:02.214 --> 00:33:05.254
You are letting us come in?

00:33:05.314 --> 00:33:06.666
Yes.

00:33:06.726 --> 00:33:09.157
Robert, come.

00:33:09.217 --> 00:33:11.028
I can't come.

00:33:11.088 --> 00:33:12.579
Come inside the house.

00:33:12.639 --> 00:33:13.119
Sorry.

00:33:13.139 --> 00:33:15.850
Oh, thank you.

00:33:15.910 --> 00:33:18.622
We are escaping from the English.

00:33:18.683 --> 00:33:19.894
I know.

00:33:19.954 --> 00:33:21.834
You are welcome here.

00:33:21.894 --> 00:33:23.406
We are friends.

00:33:23.466 --> 00:33:28.638
My husband is dying, but I don't want the English to catch him.

00:33:28.698 --> 00:33:30.239
I...

00:33:30.299 --> 00:33:32.888
Listen!

00:33:32.948 --> 00:33:36.558
They've gone.

00:33:36.618 --> 00:33:39.419
Robert, we are safe.

00:33:39.479 --> 00:33:42.180
Robert, we are safe.

00:33:42.240 --> 00:33:43.762
Safe.

00:33:43.822 --> 00:33:45.272
Safe.

00:33:45.332 --> 00:33:46.632
Safe.

00:33:46.692 --> 00:33:51.575
Safe.

00:33:51.635 --> 00:33:57.098
If disappeared.

00:33:57.158 --> 00:33:59.028
Yes.

00:33:59.088 --> 00:34:02.230
And I don't think they will come again.

00:34:02.290 --> 00:34:03.998
Jane, you...

00:34:04.058 --> 00:34:06.186
You are amazing.

00:34:06.246 --> 00:34:07.928
Thank you, Walter.

00:34:07.988 --> 00:34:10.079
I don't know what to say.

00:34:10.140 --> 00:34:12.172
Don't say anything.

00:34:12.231 --> 00:34:14.854
Welcome to your new home.

00:34:14.914 --> 00:34:18.446
I hope you spend many happy days here.

00:34:18.506 --> 00:34:20.588
I hope so too.

00:34:20.649 --> 00:34:22.850
Oh, God.

00:34:22.910 --> 00:34:24.832
I really need a whiskey now.

00:34:24.892 --> 00:34:31.046
Walter, whiskey is not a good idea for someone who's just had a heart attack.

00:34:31.106 --> 00:34:37.422
Jane, meeting the ghosts who gave me the heart attack in the first place wasn't such a good idea.

00:34:37.482 --> 00:35:04.169
If I can survive that, I can survive a glass of whiskey.

00:35:04.229 --> 00:35:33.617
The darkest night.

00:35:33.677 --> 00:35:42.183
Sophie, you awake?

00:35:42.243 --> 00:35:43.254
Yes.

00:35:43.314 --> 00:35:44.895
Can you look at the map?

00:35:44.955 --> 00:35:45.916
Sorry.

00:35:45.976 --> 00:35:46.886
Sophie, wake up.

00:35:46.906 --> 00:35:48.698
We're nearly there.

00:35:48.758 --> 00:35:51.471
Can you look at the map, please?

00:35:51.532 --> 00:35:52.432
Not map.

00:35:52.492 --> 00:35:58.408
Sophie, we've just passed a place called Mold, which means that we must be getting there to take.

00:35:58.468 --> 00:35:59.366
Where?

00:35:59.426 --> 00:36:01.634
Plus, take the place where we're going to stay.

00:36:01.674 --> 00:36:02.395
We're nearly there.

00:36:02.415 --> 00:36:05.377
So, why do I have to look on the map?

00:36:05.437 --> 00:36:08.190
Because I wrote some instructions on it.

00:36:08.250 --> 00:36:09.161
Sophie, hurry up.

00:36:09.201 --> 00:36:10.302
We may miss the turning.

00:36:10.362 --> 00:36:11.964
Tom, don't be angry with me.

00:36:12.024 --> 00:36:13.475
Well, I need your help.

00:36:13.535 --> 00:36:16.438
I can't drive and look at the map at the same time.

00:36:16.498 --> 00:36:18.269
OK, OK.

00:36:18.310 --> 00:36:18.958
Let me...

00:36:19.018 --> 00:36:20.175
What?

00:36:20.235 --> 00:36:21.276
What is it?

00:36:21.336 --> 00:36:21.886
The girl!

00:36:21.906 --> 00:36:23.306
You're going to hit that girl!

00:36:23.346 --> 00:36:24.047
What girl?

00:36:24.067 --> 00:36:25.247
The girl in the road!

00:36:25.287 --> 00:36:25.807
Look out!

00:36:25.847 --> 00:36:27.948
Sophie, take your hand off the wheel!

00:36:27.988 --> 00:36:28.308
Oh!

00:36:28.368 --> 00:36:28.828
No!

00:36:28.868 --> 00:36:32.759
No!

00:36:32.820 --> 00:36:36.611
What the hell was all that about?

00:36:36.631 --> 00:36:39.382
Are you okay?

00:36:39.442 --> 00:36:41.702
I think so.

00:36:41.763 --> 00:36:44.704
But what about the girl?

00:36:44.764 --> 00:36:45.994
Did you hit her?

00:36:46.054 --> 00:36:48.244
What on earth are you talking about?

00:36:48.304 --> 00:36:51.915
Look Sophie, I've just crashed the car into...

00:36:51.975 --> 00:36:54.106
What the hell is this?

00:36:54.166 --> 00:36:57.847
You've crashed into a great big mound of earth.

00:36:57.907 --> 00:37:01.938
There was a girl crossing the road, didn't you see her?

00:37:01.958 --> 00:37:03.479
No, I didn't see anyone.

00:37:03.539 --> 00:37:05.489
And anyway, look at the car.

00:37:05.549 --> 00:37:08.120
Oh my god, if you hit her, she could be dead.

00:37:08.140 --> 00:37:09.751
I didn't hit anyone.

00:37:09.811 --> 00:37:11.601
There was no one on the road.

00:37:11.661 --> 00:37:13.302
What's the matter with you?

00:37:13.362 --> 00:37:40.542
dreaming no I saw a girl she stepped right in front of the car and she looked straight at me it was as if she wanted to kill herself well she nearly killed us Sophie where are you going I'm going to look for her oh please God let her be okay can you see anything no Oh, there's no one here.

00:37:40.562 --> 00:37:42.964
I told you there wasn't anyone.

00:37:43.024 --> 00:37:46.038
Tom, I saw a girl.

00:37:46.098 --> 00:37:49.340
She stepped out into the road in front of the car.

00:37:49.400 --> 00:37:51.062
What did she look like?

00:37:51.122 --> 00:37:52.774
She was young.

00:37:52.834 --> 00:37:55.536
She looked about 14 and...

00:37:55.596 --> 00:37:56.797
And what?

00:37:56.857 --> 00:37:58.318
Well, she looked...

00:37:58.379 --> 00:37:59.620
I don't know.

00:37:59.680 --> 00:38:01.926
She looked old-fashioned.

00:38:01.986 --> 00:38:04.922
I've never seen anyone who looked like that.

00:38:04.982 --> 00:38:10.134
And she was carrying something, a kind of bag that looked really old.

00:38:10.194 --> 00:38:13.956
Sophie, I don't think you actually saw anyone.

00:38:14.016 --> 00:38:16.518
I think you were still half asleep.

00:38:16.578 --> 00:38:17.958
Maybe.

00:38:18.018 --> 00:38:23.250
Anyway, we have to do something about the car.

00:38:23.310 --> 00:38:28.728
Let's see if I can start it.

00:38:28.788 --> 00:38:30.372
No.

00:38:30.392 --> 00:38:36.134
Okay.

00:38:36.194 --> 00:38:43.066
Well, this car isn't going anywhere.

00:38:43.126 --> 00:38:44.736
What did we hit?

00:38:44.796 --> 00:38:49.378
Well, I thought it was just a load of earth.

00:38:49.438 --> 00:38:53.729
But it's really solid.

00:38:53.789 --> 00:38:58.298
It's some kind of round wall or something.

00:38:58.359 --> 00:38:59.697
Oh.

00:38:59.758 --> 00:39:01.348
What is it?

00:39:01.408 --> 00:39:03.490
I think it's a well.

00:39:03.550 --> 00:39:04.610
A well?

00:39:04.670 --> 00:39:05.291
What?

00:39:05.351 --> 00:39:06.522
Like the water?

00:39:06.582 --> 00:39:07.362
Yes.

00:39:07.422 --> 00:39:09.554
Well, it used to be a well.

00:39:09.614 --> 00:39:12.246
It's been filled in.

00:39:12.306 --> 00:39:13.806
Right.

00:39:13.866 --> 00:39:17.458
So, what are we going to do about the car?

00:39:17.518 --> 00:39:20.450
I'll try to call someone.

00:39:20.511 --> 00:39:22.442
Oh.

00:39:22.502 --> 00:39:23.672
What?

00:39:23.732 --> 00:39:25.464
I can't get a signal.

00:39:25.524 --> 00:39:26.344
Can you?

00:39:26.404 --> 00:39:28.749
Wait a sec.

00:39:28.809 --> 00:39:32.274
No, I can't.

00:39:32.335 --> 00:39:34.046
Not surprising, really.

00:39:34.086 --> 00:39:35.547
We're in the middle of nowhere.

00:39:35.567 --> 00:39:36.828
Oh.

00:39:36.888 --> 00:39:37.839
Look!

00:39:37.899 --> 00:39:38.489
What?

00:39:38.550 --> 00:39:40.050
The sign over there.

00:39:40.110 --> 00:39:41.371
Plus tag.

00:39:41.432 --> 00:39:42.682
Plus tag?

00:39:42.742 --> 00:39:43.383
Oh!

00:39:43.443 --> 00:39:44.854
The place where we're going to stay?

00:39:44.914 --> 00:39:46.325
Yes.

00:39:46.385 --> 00:39:49.478
It's two kilometers down that road.

00:39:49.538 --> 00:39:50.989
Two kilometers?

00:39:51.049 --> 00:39:51.960
Oh, no!

00:39:52.020 --> 00:39:53.141
It's not far.

00:39:53.201 --> 00:39:54.965
We can leave the luggage in the car.

00:39:55.025 --> 00:39:57.519
I'm not leaving anything in the car.

00:39:57.579 --> 00:39:58.980
It could get stolen.

00:39:59.040 --> 00:40:01.011
Sophie, what did you just say?

00:40:01.071 --> 00:40:02.792
We're in the middle of nowhere.

00:40:02.852 --> 00:40:05.083
No one is going to steal anything.

00:40:05.143 --> 00:40:08.795
I am not leaving anything in the car.

00:40:08.815 --> 00:40:10.346
Okay.

00:40:10.406 --> 00:40:16.924
Let's unpack and start walking.

00:40:16.984 --> 00:40:21.751
Grandma.

00:40:21.811 --> 00:40:23.452
What is it, Gwyn?

00:40:23.512 --> 00:40:26.293
There are two people walking down the path.

00:40:26.353 --> 00:40:27.513
Who are they?

00:40:27.573 --> 00:40:28.813
I don't know.

00:40:28.874 --> 00:40:32.435
They're not from round here, and they've got a lot of luggage.

00:40:32.495 --> 00:40:33.705
Really?

00:40:33.765 --> 00:40:35.236
Strange.

00:40:35.296 --> 00:40:40.067
I'm expecting some people from London, but they're coming by car.

00:40:40.127 --> 00:40:42.448
I wonder who these people are.

00:40:42.508 --> 00:40:43.688
Don't know.

00:40:43.748 --> 00:40:45.039
Well, go on.

00:40:45.099 --> 00:40:45.849
What?

00:40:45.909 --> 00:40:47.520
Go out and help them.

00:40:47.540 --> 00:40:50.606
Oh, OK.

00:40:50.666 --> 00:40:53.274
Nearly there.

00:40:53.334 --> 00:40:54.594
Oh, good.

00:40:54.654 --> 00:40:57.187
My feet are killing me.

00:40:57.247 --> 00:41:01.324
And my arms are killing me from carrying all your luggage.

00:41:01.384 --> 00:41:04.259
Can't carry suitcases in these shoes.

00:41:04.319 --> 00:41:04.889
Right.

00:41:04.949 --> 00:41:07.090
Oh, look, someone's coming.

00:41:07.150 --> 00:41:08.051
Hello?

00:41:08.111 --> 00:41:09.112
Hello?

00:41:09.172 --> 00:41:11.453
Have you come to stay at Plus Tag?

00:41:11.513 --> 00:41:12.544
Yes.

00:41:12.604 --> 00:41:15.245
Here, let me give you a hand with your luggage.

00:41:15.305 --> 00:41:16.656
Thank you very much.

00:41:16.716 --> 00:41:19.157
Flippin' heck, this one's heavy.

00:41:19.217 --> 00:41:19.998
I know.

00:41:20.058 --> 00:41:23.140
I'll take this round the back of the house and up to your room.

00:41:23.200 --> 00:41:25.641
You're in the bell and my gran will let you in.

00:41:25.701 --> 00:41:26.641
Okay.

00:41:26.702 --> 00:41:27.792
Thank you.

00:41:27.852 --> 00:41:29.304
Goodness.

00:41:29.364 --> 00:41:31.616
at this ancient bell.

00:41:31.676 --> 00:41:33.766
I wonder if it works.

00:41:33.826 --> 00:41:38.478
Yes, it does.

00:41:38.538 --> 00:41:42.589
Hello?

00:41:42.649 --> 00:41:46.511
Ah, you must be Mr. and Mrs. Parks.

00:41:46.571 --> 00:41:47.501
Is that right?

00:41:47.561 --> 00:41:48.191
Yes.

00:41:48.251 --> 00:41:52.673
Well, I'm Tom Parks and this is my partner, Sophie Richardson.

00:41:52.733 --> 00:41:53.813
Hello.

00:41:53.873 --> 00:41:56.084
Are you Mrs. Craven?

00:41:56.144 --> 00:41:57.794
Yes, that's right.

00:41:57.854 --> 00:42:00.065
Welcome to Plastig.

00:42:00.125 --> 00:42:03.717
Um, did you come by bus from Molt?

00:42:03.777 --> 00:42:07.369
No, no, we came by car.

00:42:07.429 --> 00:42:09.270
Oh, so...

00:42:09.330 --> 00:42:10.821
We had an accident.

00:42:10.881 --> 00:42:14.694
I'm afraid I crashed into the old well at the corner of the main road.

00:42:14.754 --> 00:42:17.606
You crashed into the old well?

00:42:17.666 --> 00:42:20.027
How did you manage to do that?

00:42:20.087 --> 00:42:21.288
Well, I...

00:42:21.348 --> 00:42:23.238
It's a long story.

00:42:23.298 --> 00:42:27.736
Well, come inside.

00:42:27.796 --> 00:42:32.606
Right, this is your room.

00:42:32.667 --> 00:42:34.429
It's wonderful.

00:42:34.489 --> 00:42:36.922
Yes, it's brilliant.

00:42:36.982 --> 00:42:40.827
Mrs Craven, is there a garage near here?

00:42:40.887 --> 00:42:43.250
Is there someone who can fix my car?

00:42:43.310 --> 00:42:46.014
I've already asked Gwyn to call someone.

00:42:46.074 --> 00:42:46.974
Thank you.

00:42:47.034 --> 00:42:52.586
I hope you don't mind me asking, but how did the accident happen?

00:42:52.647 --> 00:42:54.817
Well, Sophie...

00:42:54.877 --> 00:42:58.398
I thought I saw someone step into the road, Mrs Craven.

00:42:58.458 --> 00:43:00.709
I thought we were going to hit her.

00:43:00.769 --> 00:43:03.520
Someone stepped into the road?

00:43:03.580 --> 00:43:05.630
I think I was just dreaming.

00:43:05.690 --> 00:43:11.812
But you think you saw someone on the road at the junction with the road to this house?

00:43:11.872 --> 00:43:13.107
Yes.

00:43:13.168 --> 00:43:16.774
Can you describe the person that you saw?

00:43:16.834 --> 00:43:18.586
It was a girl.

00:43:18.646 --> 00:43:21.427
She was about 14?

00:43:21.487 --> 00:43:22.448
A girl?

00:43:22.468 --> 00:43:24.798
I see.

00:43:24.858 --> 00:43:28.530
Did you notice anything else about her?

00:43:28.591 --> 00:43:29.491
Yes.

00:43:29.551 --> 00:43:32.002
She was carrying an old bag.

00:43:32.062 --> 00:43:33.723
But I was half asleep.

00:43:33.783 --> 00:43:35.284
I think I was dreaming.

00:43:35.344 --> 00:43:36.144
Yes.

00:43:36.204 --> 00:43:37.475
Of course you were.

00:43:37.495 --> 00:43:45.993
Ah, here's Grin.

00:43:46.053 --> 00:43:54.800
Grant, David Gower from the garage is here to look at the car.

00:43:54.860 --> 00:43:55.911
Great.

00:43:55.971 --> 00:43:59.032
Can you give us the keys and we'll go and see what we can do?

00:43:59.092 --> 00:44:00.652
Yes, of course.

00:44:00.712 --> 00:44:01.893
Here you are.

00:44:01.953 --> 00:44:02.753
Thanks.

00:44:02.773 --> 00:44:05.974
You know what?

00:44:06.034 --> 00:44:07.255
I'm hungry.

00:44:07.315 --> 00:44:11.106
Is there a anywhere good to eat?

00:44:11.167 --> 00:44:13.527
Here it is.

00:44:13.587 --> 00:44:14.978
The Trebord Arms.

00:44:15.038 --> 00:44:16.278
Thank you.

00:44:16.338 --> 00:44:17.258
Good.

00:44:17.318 --> 00:44:19.594
I'm starving.

00:44:19.654 --> 00:44:21.740
Last three pounds.

00:44:21.800 --> 00:44:22.802
Here you are.

00:44:22.862 --> 00:44:23.513
Thank you.

00:44:23.573 --> 00:44:32.527
Enjoy your evening.

00:44:32.588 --> 00:44:34.686
It looks great.

00:44:34.746 --> 00:44:36.792
Yes, but what's the food like?

00:44:36.852 --> 00:44:38.892
Remember, we're in the middle of nowhere.

00:44:38.952 --> 00:44:40.153
Let's find out.

00:44:40.213 --> 00:44:41.293
Excuse me.

00:44:41.353 --> 00:44:42.884
Hello, can I help you?

00:44:42.944 --> 00:44:44.014
Can we see a menu?

00:44:44.074 --> 00:44:45.364
It's on the wall.

00:44:45.424 --> 00:44:46.175
Sorry?

00:44:46.235 --> 00:44:47.885
We don't have a menu.

00:44:47.945 --> 00:44:50.356
The food we do is written on the wall.

00:44:50.416 --> 00:44:51.346
Over there.

00:44:51.406 --> 00:44:52.607
Oh, right.

00:44:52.667 --> 00:44:54.157
Do you want me to combat?

00:44:54.217 --> 00:44:56.398
No, I think we can order now.

00:44:56.458 --> 00:45:00.449
I think I'll have the steak pie, please.

00:45:00.510 --> 00:45:05.797
So...

00:45:05.857 --> 00:45:14.348
That was the most boring meal I've ever had in my life.

00:45:14.408 --> 00:45:16.641
Well, have you finished?

00:45:16.701 --> 00:45:17.612
Yes, thank you.

00:45:17.672 --> 00:45:18.963
Was everything alright?

00:45:19.023 --> 00:45:19.844
Wonderful.

00:45:19.904 --> 00:45:21.166
Good.

00:45:21.226 --> 00:45:23.248
Can you tell me something?

00:45:23.308 --> 00:45:23.999
Yes.

00:45:24.059 --> 00:45:25.741
How old is this pub?

00:45:25.801 --> 00:45:27.342
Oh, it's very old.

00:45:27.402 --> 00:45:30.106
The original pub was built in 1500.

00:45:30.166 --> 00:45:31.998
1500.

00:45:32.058 --> 00:45:33.229
That's amazing.

00:45:33.289 --> 00:45:39.305
Well, that building burned down a long time ago, but this place is about 300 years old.

00:45:39.365 --> 00:45:42.708
And why is it called the Trevor Arms?

00:45:42.768 --> 00:45:46.952
Ah, well, it's named after the Trevor family.

00:45:47.012 --> 00:45:49.866
They used to be the landowners around here.

00:45:49.926 --> 00:45:53.479
They lived in a big house near here called Plasteg.

00:45:53.539 --> 00:45:54.070
Oh!

00:45:54.130 --> 00:45:56.411
We're staying there, really.

00:45:56.471 --> 00:45:58.462
And is everything...

00:45:58.522 --> 00:46:00.954
is everything all right there?

00:46:01.014 --> 00:46:03.265
Yes, everything's fine.

00:46:03.325 --> 00:46:04.646
Why did you ask?

00:46:04.706 --> 00:46:05.657
Nothing.

00:46:05.717 --> 00:46:07.518
Excuse me.

00:46:07.578 --> 00:46:10.019
What was that about?

00:46:10.079 --> 00:46:11.810
What was what about?

00:46:11.870 --> 00:46:15.392
She seemed surprised that we were staying at Pla's tag.

00:46:15.452 --> 00:46:16.343
Did she?

00:46:16.403 --> 00:46:18.524
She seemed quite okay to me.

00:46:18.584 --> 00:46:20.165
Anyway, shall we go?

00:46:20.185 --> 00:46:21.236
Okay.

00:46:21.296 --> 00:46:22.426
I'll just...

00:46:22.466 --> 00:46:22.937
Tom.

00:46:22.997 --> 00:46:23.566
What?

00:46:23.626 --> 00:46:24.265
Look!

00:46:24.325 --> 00:46:24.896
What?

00:46:24.956 --> 00:46:25.906
At the window!

00:46:25.966 --> 00:46:27.027
What is it now?

00:46:27.067 --> 00:46:29.168
That girl again!

00:46:29.228 --> 00:46:33.941
Sophie, come back!

00:46:34.001 --> 00:46:37.173
What are you doing?

00:46:37.193 --> 00:46:39.114
I saw that girl again!

00:46:39.134 --> 00:46:39.874
The witch girl!

00:46:39.914 --> 00:46:42.156
The girl we nearly ran down in the road!

00:46:42.216 --> 00:46:43.587
She was at the window!

00:46:43.647 --> 00:46:44.527
Where is she now?

00:46:44.587 --> 00:46:45.728
I don't know!

00:46:45.788 --> 00:46:47.159
She disappeared again!

00:46:47.179 --> 00:46:48.900
I think she's in the woods!

00:46:48.960 --> 00:46:50.611
Sophie, come back!

00:46:50.671 --> 00:46:52.232
I've got to find her!

00:46:52.292 --> 00:46:53.559
Stop!

00:46:53.619 --> 00:46:58.228
Sophie!

00:46:58.288 --> 00:47:02.791
What the hell is going on?

00:47:02.851 --> 00:47:04.172
I don't know!

00:47:04.232 --> 00:47:05.903
Jesus!

00:47:05.923 --> 00:47:06.904
Tom!

00:47:06.964 --> 00:47:08.525
I'm scared!

00:47:08.585 --> 00:47:09.065
Wait, Tom!

00:47:09.105 --> 00:47:09.516
Tom!

00:47:09.576 --> 00:47:10.036
What?

00:47:10.096 --> 00:47:11.877
Look out!

00:47:11.937 --> 00:47:14.099
Oh God!

00:47:14.159 --> 00:47:15.069
Are you all right?

00:47:15.089 --> 00:47:15.840
No!

00:47:15.900 --> 00:47:16.800
Wait here!

00:47:16.860 --> 00:47:17.631
I'll get help!

00:47:17.651 --> 00:47:19.982
Go away!

00:47:20.042 --> 00:47:21.644
Who's there?

00:47:21.704 --> 00:47:24.166
Go away!

00:47:24.226 --> 00:47:25.758
Tom!

00:47:25.819 --> 00:47:27.180
It's the girl!

00:47:27.240 --> 00:47:31.346
Go away, I've never come in again.

00:47:31.406 --> 00:47:35.911
If you do, something even worse will happen.

00:47:35.971 --> 00:47:38.565
Ah!

00:47:38.625 --> 00:47:41.032
Tom.

00:47:41.092 --> 00:47:42.960
Where am I?

00:47:43.020 --> 00:47:44.601
You're in hospital.

00:47:44.662 --> 00:47:46.074
In hospital?

00:47:46.134 --> 00:47:46.854
What?

00:47:46.915 --> 00:47:47.456
Oh!

00:47:47.516 --> 00:47:48.998
Don't try to move.

00:47:49.058 --> 00:47:51.251
What's the matter with me?

00:47:51.311 --> 00:47:55.176
You have a broken shoulder and a broken arm.

00:47:55.236 --> 00:47:56.929
You're lucky to be alive.

00:47:56.949 --> 00:47:59.789
What happened?

00:47:59.849 --> 00:48:02.719
Yeah.

00:48:02.779 --> 00:48:04.752
I remember now.

00:48:04.812 --> 00:48:08.105
Well, at least it wasn't that girl.

00:48:08.166 --> 00:48:09.568
It was that girl.

00:48:09.628 --> 00:48:11.800
I'm sure she was responsible.

00:48:11.860 --> 00:48:18.474
If you ever come near me again, something even worse will happen.

00:48:18.534 --> 00:48:23.044
When we were in the woods, she was there.

00:48:23.104 --> 00:48:26.626
When the tree fell on you, she was there.

00:48:26.686 --> 00:48:27.927
Sophie, listen.

00:48:27.947 --> 00:48:28.588
No, Tom.

00:48:28.648 --> 00:48:30.228
You listen to me.

00:48:30.288 --> 00:48:33.962
I am not the only one who has seen this girl.

00:48:34.022 --> 00:48:36.594
Everyone around here knows about her.

00:48:36.654 --> 00:48:40.817
That's why the waitress in the pub wanted to know if everything was all right.

00:48:40.877 --> 00:48:41.467
What?

00:48:41.527 --> 00:48:42.178
Waitress.

00:48:42.238 --> 00:48:45.510
And terrible things always happen when she appears.

00:48:45.570 --> 00:48:47.432
How do you know all this?

00:48:47.492 --> 00:48:49.734
Mrs Craven told me.

00:48:49.794 --> 00:48:51.295
She's here.

00:48:51.356 --> 00:48:54.939
And she wants to tell us the whole story.

00:48:54.999 --> 00:48:57.422
Are you ready for this?

00:48:57.482 --> 00:48:59.264
I guess so.

00:48:59.324 --> 00:49:04.563
I'll go and get her.

00:49:04.623 --> 00:49:10.032
Hello, Mrs. Craven.

00:49:10.092 --> 00:49:13.493
Mr. Parks, I'm so sorry.

00:49:13.553 --> 00:49:15.374
Don't be silly, Mrs. Craven.

00:49:15.434 --> 00:49:16.834
This isn't your fault.

00:49:16.894 --> 00:49:19.235
Well, maybe it is.

00:49:19.295 --> 00:49:20.386
Why?

00:49:20.446 --> 00:49:21.846
What do you mean?

00:49:21.906 --> 00:49:24.797
I should have warned you about the girl.

00:49:24.857 --> 00:49:28.308
Mrs. Craven, tell Tom what you told me.

00:49:28.368 --> 00:49:36.090
The girl that Sophie saw is someone who lived in my house 500 years ago.

00:49:36.150 --> 00:49:44.006
The house was built by a man called Sir John Trevo, sometime around 1500.

00:49:44.066 --> 00:49:50.732
When he died, his brother Edward became the owner of the house.

00:49:50.792 --> 00:49:55.668
Ashes to ashes, dust to dust.

00:49:55.728 --> 00:50:01.310
We commended our dear brother to the earth.

00:50:01.370 --> 00:50:08.532
My Lord, therefore, allow me to express my deepest sympathy.

00:50:08.592 --> 00:50:10.604
Thank you, Squirt Welling.

00:50:10.664 --> 00:50:16.640
My Lord, is it true that you and your family will now live at Plastang?

00:50:16.700 --> 00:50:18.812
Correct, Squirt Welling.

00:50:18.872 --> 00:50:27.584
And in a few weeks' time, when we have finished mourning, my dear brother John, we will have a feast and invite people from all over the county.

00:50:27.644 --> 00:50:33.432
And is it also true that your daughter Dorothy is already 16?

00:50:33.492 --> 00:50:35.763
She is indeed in fact.

00:50:35.823 --> 00:50:40.226
She will be 17 in just a few months, I see.

00:50:40.286 --> 00:50:45.860
Did you know that my son Alan finds her most desirable?

00:50:45.920 --> 00:50:48.292
I knew of this, Clewellyn.

00:50:48.351 --> 00:50:57.017
It occurred to me that we may use the occasion of the feast to announce the betrudal of my son and your daughter.

00:50:57.077 --> 00:51:00.588
This was my idea too.

00:51:00.649 --> 00:51:01.789
Dorothy?

00:51:01.849 --> 00:51:03.100
Yes, Father.

00:51:03.160 --> 00:51:05.801
I'm going to make an announcement to the servants.

00:51:05.861 --> 00:51:08.402
I would like you to be there when I do it.

00:51:08.462 --> 00:51:13.984
Yes, Father.

00:51:14.044 --> 00:51:20.402
Good morning, everyone.

00:51:20.462 --> 00:51:30.313
I, Edward Trefor, am now master of Plasté, and I want you to know that life in the great house will continue as before.

00:51:30.374 --> 00:51:34.266
Everyone will continue to do the work they are doing now.

00:51:34.326 --> 00:51:41.978
For now, the house is in mourning for my dear brother.

00:51:42.038 --> 00:52:01.207
Very soon we will have a great feast of celebration, and the cause of celebration will be the announcement of the marriage of my daughter Dorothy to Alan Clewellyn.

00:52:01.267 --> 00:52:08.600
Young Miss Dorothy is to marry Alan Llewellyn.

00:52:08.660 --> 00:52:10.680
I cannot believe it.

00:52:10.741 --> 00:52:13.992
Alan Llewellyn, such a horrible man.

00:52:14.052 --> 00:52:16.863
And did you see the young girl's face?

00:52:16.923 --> 00:52:19.514
She didn't look very happy about the idea.

00:52:19.574 --> 00:52:20.665
You're right.

00:52:20.725 --> 00:52:25.666
She looked shocked.

00:52:25.726 --> 00:52:35.326
So Dorothy, you are to be married in June on the occasion of your 17th birthday.

00:52:35.386 --> 00:52:39.342
Father, this is not what I expected.

00:52:39.402 --> 00:52:41.493
Not what you expected.

00:52:41.553 --> 00:52:42.743
What do you mean?

00:52:42.803 --> 00:52:46.434
I feel I am not ready for marriage.

00:52:46.495 --> 00:52:47.925
Not ready.

00:52:47.985 --> 00:52:50.976
Dorothy, you're nearly 17.

00:52:51.036 --> 00:52:58.085
Nearly halfway through your life, of course, you are ready.

00:52:58.145 --> 00:53:04.914
Well, Miss Dorothy, you are to be married.

00:53:04.974 --> 00:53:06.084
Annie, listen.

00:53:06.144 --> 00:53:06.984
Yes, Miss.

00:53:07.044 --> 00:53:09.514
You are the only person I can trust.

00:53:09.574 --> 00:53:10.825
Yes, Miss.

00:53:10.885 --> 00:53:14.245
You know that I do not love Alan Joellen.

00:53:14.305 --> 00:53:16.126
Oh, Miss Dorothy.

00:53:16.186 --> 00:53:19.026
I am in love with Yvonne Turner.

00:53:19.086 --> 00:53:21.066
Yvonne Turner?

00:53:21.126 --> 00:53:24.847
But Yvonne Turner is just a farm hand.

00:53:24.907 --> 00:53:27.007
And you are a lady.

00:53:27.067 --> 00:53:28.688
Annie, I love him.

00:53:28.708 --> 00:53:35.109
I will not marry Alan Joellen.

00:53:35.169 --> 00:53:41.270
Ivan, are you there?

00:53:41.330 --> 00:53:42.281
Yes.

00:53:42.341 --> 00:53:45.202
Oh, Ivan, hold me.

00:53:45.262 --> 00:53:49.332
Ivan, why are you so cold with me?

00:53:49.392 --> 00:53:52.203
Because you are to marry Alan Thorellen.

00:53:52.263 --> 00:53:56.074
Ivan, I do not wish to marry Alan Thorellen.

00:53:56.134 --> 00:53:58.295
This is my father's idea.

00:53:58.355 --> 00:54:00.826
It is you who I wish to marry.

00:54:00.886 --> 00:54:03.106
Your father is Lord of the Mananaur.

00:54:03.166 --> 00:54:06.426
He will never allow you to marry someone who works on the land.

00:54:06.486 --> 00:54:09.146
I don't care about my father's wishes.

00:54:09.206 --> 00:54:11.046
I will marry you.

00:54:11.106 --> 00:54:13.777
Dorothy, that is impossible now.

00:54:13.837 --> 00:54:15.687
No, it isn't.

00:54:15.747 --> 00:54:18.058
We would go away from here.

00:54:18.118 --> 00:54:19.258
Go away?

00:54:19.318 --> 00:54:20.679
Where can we go?

00:54:20.739 --> 00:54:22.119
And how will we live?

00:54:22.179 --> 00:54:25.380
We can find somewhere where we can be safe.

00:54:25.440 --> 00:54:27.200
And we will live well.

00:54:27.260 --> 00:54:28.631
I have some jewels.

00:54:28.691 --> 00:54:30.036
We can sell them.

00:54:30.096 --> 00:54:34.384
Sell your jewels, Dorothy, this idea is mad.

00:54:34.444 --> 00:54:37.297
Ivan, do you want me for your wife?

00:54:37.357 --> 00:54:38.338
Of course.

00:54:38.398 --> 00:54:41.200
In that case, we must go away.

00:54:41.220 --> 00:54:42.221
When?

00:54:42.281 --> 00:54:43.062
Soon.

00:54:43.122 --> 00:54:45.954
They want me to marry on my 17th birthday.

00:54:46.014 --> 00:54:54.819
In June, we have time, and I have a plan.

00:54:54.879 --> 00:55:03.241
My Lord Edward, this is a fine feast.

00:55:03.301 --> 00:55:05.212
Thank you, Chloe.

00:55:05.272 --> 00:55:09.193
Will you make the announcement of the marriage dates this evening?

00:55:09.253 --> 00:55:11.224
Indeed, I will.

00:55:11.284 --> 00:55:19.906
Lord Edward, I think it would be a fine idea if the wedding took place sooner rather than later.

00:55:19.966 --> 00:55:20.966
Really?

00:55:21.026 --> 00:55:22.484
Why?

00:55:22.544 --> 00:55:26.201
I have heard rumours that Dorothy is...

00:55:26.262 --> 00:55:28.583
Well, how can I say?

00:55:28.643 --> 00:55:32.836
Very friendly with a young man in the village.

00:55:32.896 --> 00:55:39.660
A young man in the village who is a farm hand named Yifan Turner.

00:55:39.720 --> 00:55:41.341
Yifan Turner?

00:55:41.401 --> 00:55:42.982
I know the boy.

00:55:43.042 --> 00:55:44.703
He has worked on my land.

00:55:44.763 --> 00:55:45.623
Yes.

00:55:45.684 --> 00:55:47.895
He has worked on my land also.

00:55:47.955 --> 00:55:50.133
This cannot be possible.

00:55:50.193 --> 00:55:52.982
It is only something I have heard.

00:55:53.042 --> 00:55:59.358
Perhaps we should consider holding the wedding ceremony sooner than daughter his 17th ward.

00:55:59.418 --> 00:56:00.630
Indeed.

00:56:00.690 --> 00:56:03.832
The wedding must take place as soon as possible.

00:56:03.893 --> 00:56:08.126
Let us say, Saturday week, 10 days from now.

00:56:08.186 --> 00:56:10.428
This is a fine idea, my dear.

00:56:10.488 --> 00:56:13.041
I will make the announcement now.

00:56:13.101 --> 00:56:24.116
Ladies and gentlemen, Ladies and gentlemen, I trust that you find my humble feast to your liking.

00:56:24.176 --> 00:56:42.500
I wish to take this opportunity to announce that the marriage of my daughter, Dorothy, to Alan Schlewellen, the son of my friend, Schlewellen, will take place here at Plaste in ten days' time.

00:56:42.560 --> 00:56:44.891
What is going on there?

00:56:44.952 --> 00:56:47.000
It's your daughter, Dorothy.

00:56:47.060 --> 00:56:51.610
She has fainted.

00:56:51.670 --> 00:56:56.914
Are you all right, Miss Dorothy?

00:56:56.974 --> 00:56:58.515
Anna, you have to help me.

00:56:58.575 --> 00:56:59.876
Help you?

00:56:59.936 --> 00:57:01.748
What do you wish me to do?

00:57:01.808 --> 00:57:06.911
Tonight I want you to go to the village and I want you to take this bag.

00:57:06.971 --> 00:57:08.232
What is it?

00:57:08.292 --> 00:57:10.074
Look inside.

00:57:10.134 --> 00:57:12.655
Goodness, Miss Dorothy.

00:57:12.715 --> 00:57:14.926
These are all your jewels.

00:57:14.986 --> 00:57:17.387
What do you wish me to do with them?

00:57:17.447 --> 00:57:21.248
I want you to take the jewels to Ivan Turner's house.

00:57:21.308 --> 00:57:23.209
To Ivan's house?

00:57:23.269 --> 00:57:24.380
But why?

00:57:24.440 --> 00:57:27.311
Please don't ask any questions.

00:57:27.371 --> 00:57:34.594
I want you to tell Ivan to meet me where the road from plastic meets the road to mold.

00:57:34.654 --> 00:57:39.469
Near the well, tell him to meet me there tomorrow night at midnight.

00:57:39.529 --> 00:57:43.503
Miss Jhaarithi, what are you thinking of?

00:57:43.563 --> 00:57:47.447
Ani, I cannot marry Squaehuel and Sun.

00:57:47.508 --> 00:57:49.910
Ivan and I are going to run away.

00:57:49.930 --> 00:57:56.502
Oh, Miss Jhaarithi!

00:57:56.562 --> 00:58:07.594
The next evening, Squire Joellen and his son Alan came to plus take for dinner.

00:58:07.654 --> 00:58:12.366
Dorothy said she felt ill and asked to be excused.

00:58:12.426 --> 00:58:16.981
When she left the room, Alan followed her.

00:58:17.041 --> 00:58:18.905
Dorothy!

00:58:18.965 --> 00:58:20.165
Dorothy!

00:58:20.226 --> 00:58:21.956
Why do you avoid me?

00:58:22.016 --> 00:58:24.717
I am not avoiding you, Mr. Clewellyn!

00:58:24.777 --> 00:58:26.407
Mr. Clewellyn!

00:58:26.467 --> 00:58:27.547
Dorothy!

00:58:27.608 --> 00:58:29.218
We are to be married!

00:58:29.278 --> 00:58:31.248
You can call me Alan!

00:58:31.308 --> 00:58:33.449
And maybe you should allow me to...

00:58:33.489 --> 00:58:35.149
Take your hands off me!

00:58:35.209 --> 00:58:36.300
Come, come, Dorothy!

00:58:36.360 --> 00:58:38.520
I said take your hands off me!

00:58:38.580 --> 00:58:39.820
Well...

00:58:39.880 --> 00:58:41.359
Dorothy...

00:58:41.419 --> 00:58:44.042
You had better change your attitude quickly.

00:58:44.102 --> 00:58:46.700
We are to be married in nine days.

00:58:46.720 --> 00:58:50.140
Leave me alone!

00:58:50.200 --> 00:58:56.560
Dorothy didn't want to spend another minute in the house.

00:58:56.620 --> 00:59:04.456
She closed her bedroom door, changed into some warm clothes and put a few possessions in a small bag.

00:59:04.516 --> 00:59:08.668
She walked down the back staircase and quietly left the house.

00:59:08.728 --> 00:59:14.012
Her plan was to wait in the woods near the well until Yvonne arrived.

00:59:14.072 --> 00:59:23.434
But when she reached the edge of the woods, she heard the sound of a horse approaching.

00:59:23.494 --> 00:59:28.104
Ivan.

00:59:28.164 --> 00:59:29.975
Ivan, is it you?

00:59:30.035 --> 00:59:31.415
Ivan?

00:59:31.476 --> 00:59:33.796
No, Dorothy, this is Alan.

00:59:33.856 --> 00:59:35.027
Mr. who Alan?

00:59:35.087 --> 00:59:36.538
What are you doing here?

00:59:36.598 --> 00:59:38.468
What am I doing here?

00:59:38.528 --> 00:59:41.739
Surely I could ask you the same question, Mr. Vore.

00:59:41.800 --> 00:59:43.890
What are you doing here?

00:59:43.950 --> 00:59:46.851
I am waiting to meet the man I love.

00:59:46.912 --> 00:59:48.822
The man you love?

00:59:48.882 --> 00:59:50.968
What are you talking about?

00:59:51.028 --> 00:59:57.288
Who, pray, tell me is the man you love, if you remember you and I are to marry.

00:59:57.348 --> 01:00:00.180
I will not marry you, Mr. Chuelen.

01:00:00.240 --> 01:00:02.132
I am in love with another.

01:00:02.192 --> 01:00:03.263
Who?

01:00:03.323 --> 01:00:05.124
Who are you in love with?

01:00:05.185 --> 01:00:07.994
I am in love with Yvonne Turner.

01:00:08.054 --> 01:00:10.134
Evantana.

01:00:10.194 --> 01:00:12.857
He's just a farm boy.

01:00:12.917 --> 01:00:15.810
You cannot love a farm boy.

01:00:15.830 --> 01:00:19.764
I can, and I do, and I will marry him too.

01:00:19.824 --> 01:00:21.196
Are you mad?

01:00:21.256 --> 01:00:23.589
You are going to marry me.

01:00:23.649 --> 01:00:25.851
Take your hands off me.

01:00:25.912 --> 01:00:30.616
I could never marry an ugly brute such as you.

01:00:30.676 --> 01:00:36.529
Don't ever hit me again or you will admit it!

01:00:36.549 --> 01:00:37.409
Go away!

01:00:37.429 --> 01:00:41.391
Go away and never come near me again!

01:00:41.451 --> 01:00:44.932
If you do, something even worse will happen!

01:00:44.992 --> 01:00:48.863
Go away and never come near me again!

01:00:48.923 --> 01:00:55.675
If you do, something even worse will happen!

01:00:55.695 --> 01:00:58.136
Oh dear, you talk to me like that!

01:00:58.196 --> 01:01:00.016
I will teach you a lesson!

01:01:00.076 --> 01:01:02.648
Take your hands off me!

01:01:02.708 --> 01:01:09.684
Get off me!

01:01:09.744 --> 01:01:14.036
Oh my god!

01:01:14.096 --> 01:01:15.407
Dorothy!

01:01:15.467 --> 01:01:18.193
Dorothy!

01:01:18.253 --> 01:01:20.949
What happened?

01:01:21.009 --> 01:01:23.920
Dorothy fell down the well.

01:01:23.980 --> 01:01:26.112
Didn't he try to save her?

01:01:26.172 --> 01:01:28.264
She made no sound.

01:01:28.324 --> 01:01:29.975
She was dead.

01:01:30.035 --> 01:01:32.286
So, what did he do?

01:01:32.346 --> 01:01:34.808
Did he tell anyone what had happened?

01:01:34.868 --> 01:01:36.719
He told no one.

01:01:36.780 --> 01:01:38.310
He rode away.

01:01:38.330 --> 01:01:44.995
Adi?

01:01:45.055 --> 01:01:46.492
Yes, my lord.

01:01:46.552 --> 01:01:48.058
Where is Miss Dorothy?

01:01:48.118 --> 01:01:49.509
Have you seen her this morning?

01:01:49.569 --> 01:01:50.880
No, my lord.

01:01:50.940 --> 01:01:53.812
It's very late for her to still be in her room.

01:01:53.872 --> 01:01:56.713
Please go and tell her I wish to speak to her.

01:01:56.773 --> 01:02:05.799
Yes, my lord.

01:02:05.859 --> 01:02:15.460
Miss Dorothy?

01:02:15.520 --> 01:02:19.486
Miss Dorothy, are you there?

01:02:19.546 --> 01:02:22.967
Miss Dorothy?

01:02:23.027 --> 01:02:27.059
Oh, Miss Dorothy.

01:02:27.119 --> 01:02:40.745
What have you done?

01:02:40.805 --> 01:02:43.286
Squirtly, Ellen.

01:02:43.346 --> 01:02:45.464
It is good that you came so quickly.

01:02:45.524 --> 01:02:47.844
We came as soon as we heard the news.

01:02:47.904 --> 01:02:49.787
Is there any sign of Dorothy?

01:02:49.847 --> 01:02:50.478
No.

01:02:50.538 --> 01:02:51.920
And there is some more news.

01:02:51.980 --> 01:02:54.603
We have discovered that all her jewelry is missing.

01:02:54.664 --> 01:02:56.476
Her jewelry is missing.

01:02:56.536 --> 01:02:58.478
This is all very suspicious.

01:02:58.538 --> 01:02:59.420
Father?

01:02:59.480 --> 01:03:00.370
Yes, Alan.

01:03:00.430 --> 01:03:02.714
I have something I wish to say.

01:03:02.774 --> 01:03:04.666
What do you wish to say, Alan?

01:03:04.726 --> 01:03:06.576
My lord, Trevor.

01:03:06.636 --> 01:03:12.699
When I left her house last night, I saw a man and a woman near the well on the mould road.

01:03:12.759 --> 01:03:19.022
I'm almost certain that the man was a farm boy from the village called Ivan Turner.

01:03:19.082 --> 01:03:20.332
Ivan Turner?

01:03:20.392 --> 01:03:21.332
Yes.

01:03:21.392 --> 01:03:22.863
What about the woman?

01:03:22.923 --> 01:03:30.086
Well, the woman looked a little like Dorothy, but I thought, of course, it couldn't be Dorothy.

01:03:30.146 --> 01:03:31.608
What were the people doing?

01:03:31.668 --> 01:03:34.670
The man appeared to be threatening the woman.

01:03:34.730 --> 01:03:37.452
When they saw me, they moved away into the trees.

01:03:37.512 --> 01:03:38.742
Did you speak to them?

01:03:38.803 --> 01:03:39.583
No.

01:03:39.643 --> 01:03:41.965
Why didn't you come to the house to tell us?

01:03:42.025 --> 01:03:44.606
Edward, why should he have done that?

01:03:44.667 --> 01:03:47.108
They were not on your land.

01:03:47.168 --> 01:03:58.286
Maybe we should go to the woods to see if we can find something.

01:03:58.346 --> 01:04:08.331
Alan, tell me, where did you see these people?

01:04:08.391 --> 01:04:10.532
They were standing by the well.

01:04:10.592 --> 01:04:12.803
Look, at the top of the well.

01:04:12.863 --> 01:04:13.804
What is that?

01:04:13.864 --> 01:04:14.714
Let me look.

01:04:14.774 --> 01:04:15.644
It's...

01:04:15.705 --> 01:04:17.885
It's a piece of torn clothing.

01:04:17.945 --> 01:04:19.726
Let me have a look.

01:04:19.786 --> 01:04:22.347
Oh, look, the well in...

01:04:22.407 --> 01:04:25.318
Look, at the bottom of the well.

01:04:25.379 --> 01:04:26.689
What can you see?

01:04:26.709 --> 01:04:28.340
I can see nothing.

01:04:28.400 --> 01:04:29.780
I can see...

01:04:29.841 --> 01:04:37.219
a body.

01:04:37.279 --> 01:04:46.529
Where is he?

01:04:46.589 --> 01:04:48.670
He is in the fields west of the village.

01:04:48.690 --> 01:04:56.130
What happened to even?

01:04:56.190 --> 01:05:05.802
He was arrested and charged with the murder of Dorothy.

01:05:05.862 --> 01:05:07.263
My God.

01:05:07.323 --> 01:05:08.204
Yes.

01:05:08.264 --> 01:05:12.395
They also found her jewelry in his house, didn't they, Mrs. Craven?

01:05:12.456 --> 01:05:17.198
They thought that he'd argued with her, killed her, and stolen her jewelry.

01:05:17.258 --> 01:05:18.279
Terrible.

01:05:18.339 --> 01:05:19.730
What happened to him?

01:05:19.790 --> 01:05:21.190
He was hanged.

01:05:21.250 --> 01:05:23.092
But what about Annie?

01:05:23.152 --> 01:05:25.483
Didn't she tell people what she knew?

01:05:25.543 --> 01:05:28.304
She was too frightened to say anything.

01:05:28.364 --> 01:05:30.576
She thought she would get into trouble.

01:05:30.636 --> 01:05:32.037
What happened to her?

01:05:32.097 --> 01:05:36.040
A few months later, she drowned in the river.

01:05:36.100 --> 01:05:38.572
People think she took her own life.

01:05:38.632 --> 01:05:41.313
So how did anyone find out the truth?

01:05:41.374 --> 01:05:46.317
Well, Alan Schlewellyn eventually married and had two sons.

01:05:46.377 --> 01:05:57.120
But when his wife then had a baby daughter, the ghost of Dorothy appeared, she told Alan he would go to hell for what he'd done.

01:05:57.180 --> 01:06:01.868
Eventually, he confessed and he was sent to jail.

01:06:01.928 --> 01:06:03.649
Did they hang him too?

01:06:03.709 --> 01:06:04.379
No.

01:06:04.439 --> 01:06:09.121
You see, two people couldn't be hanged for the same crime.

01:06:09.181 --> 01:06:11.992
And what happened when he came out of jail?

01:06:12.053 --> 01:06:13.954
He never came out.

01:06:14.014 --> 01:06:16.074
He died in jail.

01:06:16.134 --> 01:06:17.545
I see.

01:06:17.605 --> 01:06:19.826
And Dorothy's ghost.

01:06:19.886 --> 01:06:21.911
Has she been around ever since?

01:06:21.971 --> 01:06:31.498
Well, Alan Shlewellyn's wife and family moved away and the ghost was never seen again until...

01:06:31.558 --> 01:06:33.358
Until what?

01:06:33.418 --> 01:06:38.710
She appeared again, about 75 years ago.

01:06:38.770 --> 01:06:42.020
And she has appeared many times since.

01:06:42.080 --> 01:06:43.150
Really?

01:06:43.210 --> 01:06:45.431
Does anyone know why?

01:06:45.491 --> 01:06:46.822
Oh yes.

01:06:46.882 --> 01:06:49.334
We know why.

01:06:49.394 --> 01:06:57.680
You see, 75 years ago, a family called Shlewellen came to live in mold.

01:06:57.740 --> 01:07:01.911
They were direct descendants of Alan Shlewellen.

01:07:01.971 --> 01:07:06.754
Soon after they arrived, they had a child, a daughter.

01:07:06.814 --> 01:07:10.646
Dorothy appeared when the child was born.

01:07:10.706 --> 01:07:12.337
Her strange?

01:07:12.397 --> 01:07:14.288
Yes, it is strange.

01:07:14.348 --> 01:07:18.381
And she's appeared on other occasions since then, too.

01:07:18.441 --> 01:07:21.813
But go on, Mrs. Craven.

01:07:21.873 --> 01:07:24.044
Tell Tom what you told me.

01:07:24.104 --> 01:07:33.040
Well, the thing is, she always appears when descendants of the Clewellyn family are here.

01:07:33.100 --> 01:07:35.280
How strange.

01:07:35.340 --> 01:07:37.940
Well, Mr. Parks.

01:07:38.000 --> 01:07:40.384
Tom, please call me Tom.

01:07:40.444 --> 01:07:44.070
Well, Tom, you need to rest.

01:07:44.130 --> 01:07:48.758
The doctor told me that they're going to keep you in hospital overnight.

01:07:48.818 --> 01:07:50.362
I suppose...

01:07:50.422 --> 01:07:54.927
Well, will you be coming back to Plastague when they let you out?

01:07:54.987 --> 01:07:56.127
Well, I...

01:07:56.187 --> 01:07:57.948
Of course we will, Mrs. Craven.

01:07:58.008 --> 01:07:59.558
Oh, I'm so pleased.

01:07:59.618 --> 01:08:02.870
And Sophie, will you come back tonight?

01:08:02.930 --> 01:08:05.471
Or will you stay here in the hospital?

01:08:05.531 --> 01:08:06.911
I'll come back tonight.

01:08:06.971 --> 01:08:07.832
Okay.

01:08:07.892 --> 01:08:14.744
Well, give Mr. Jenkins the taxi driver a call when you're ready to leave and he'll come and pick you up.

01:08:14.804 --> 01:08:15.684
Thanks.

01:08:15.745 --> 01:08:17.685
See you later.

01:08:17.745 --> 01:08:22.938
Sophie, you aren't going back to Plus Take by yourself.

01:08:22.998 --> 01:08:23.929
Yes, I am.

01:08:23.989 --> 01:08:25.080
I have to.

01:08:25.140 --> 01:08:27.161
What do you mean you have to?

01:08:27.221 --> 01:08:28.892
Why do you have to go back?

01:08:28.952 --> 01:08:35.337
Mrs Craven already told me that Dorothy appears when there are people from the Llewellyn family.

01:08:35.396 --> 01:08:38.298
She appeared because we came here.

01:08:38.359 --> 01:08:39.480
What?

01:08:39.540 --> 01:08:41.441
Why would she do that?

01:08:41.501 --> 01:08:44.629
My name is Parks and your name is Richardson.

01:08:44.689 --> 01:08:56.178
What?

01:08:56.238 --> 01:09:09.540
She said her mother was born here.

01:09:09.600 --> 01:09:10.631
What?

01:09:10.691 --> 01:09:15.642
My grandmother was born here, 75 years ago.

01:09:15.702 --> 01:09:18.053
She was the girl child.

01:09:18.113 --> 01:09:21.724
Dorothy appeared again where my grandmother was born.

01:09:21.744 --> 01:09:24.594
Alright, let's get out of here.

01:09:24.654 --> 01:09:29.075
You aren't going anywhere, and I'm going back to Pla's Tea.

01:09:29.135 --> 01:09:32.306
Sophie, you aren't going back by yourself.

01:09:32.346 --> 01:09:34.256
Yes, I am.

01:09:34.316 --> 01:09:36.133
Yes?

01:09:36.193 --> 01:09:38.210
Miss Richardson?

01:09:38.270 --> 01:09:38.921
Yes?

01:09:38.981 --> 01:09:40.752
Your taxi has arrived.

01:09:40.812 --> 01:09:41.643
Taxi?

01:09:41.703 --> 01:09:43.104
We didn't order a taxi.

01:09:43.124 --> 01:09:44.225
Thank you, Nurse.

01:09:44.286 --> 01:09:47.498
Could you ask Mr Jenkins to wait for a few moments?

01:09:47.558 --> 01:09:49.279
Of course.

01:09:49.340 --> 01:09:51.282
Sophie?

01:09:51.341 --> 01:09:52.772
It's okay.

01:09:52.832 --> 01:09:54.574
I ordered the taxi earlier.

01:09:54.634 --> 01:09:56.256
I'm going back.

01:09:56.316 --> 01:10:00.980
Sophie, if you're planning to spend the night at Plastique, I'm coming with you.

01:10:01.040 --> 01:10:01.850
You can't.

01:10:01.910 --> 01:10:03.101
They won't let you.

01:10:03.161 --> 01:10:04.502
Goodbye, Tom.

01:10:04.562 --> 01:10:05.883
Sophie.

01:10:05.943 --> 01:10:07.324
Don't worry about me.

01:10:07.384 --> 01:10:09.006
I know what I'm doing.

01:10:09.066 --> 01:10:13.799
I'll see you tomorrow.

01:10:13.859 --> 01:10:18.172
Miss Richardson?

01:10:18.232 --> 01:10:18.993
Yes.

01:10:19.053 --> 01:10:22.216
OK.

01:10:22.276 --> 01:10:27.460
So it's back to plastic, right?

01:10:27.520 --> 01:10:28.321
Right.

01:10:28.381 --> 01:10:30.042
But not all the way.

01:10:30.102 --> 01:10:31.083
I'm sorry?

01:10:31.143 --> 01:10:33.958
I don't want you to take me all the way.

01:10:34.018 --> 01:10:35.624
Where do you want me to take you?

01:10:35.684 --> 01:10:37.106
Just leave me at the corner.

01:10:37.166 --> 01:10:38.116
Which corner?

01:10:38.177 --> 01:10:41.650
The corner of the road to Plastake, near the old well.

01:10:41.710 --> 01:10:42.802
Are you sure?

01:10:42.862 --> 01:10:47.738
Yes, I'm sure.

01:10:47.798 --> 01:10:52.640
Thank you, Mr. Jenkins.

01:10:52.700 --> 01:10:56.927
Mrs. Richardson, I don't like the idea of leaving you here.

01:10:56.987 --> 01:10:57.768
Why don't I...

01:10:57.788 --> 01:10:59.678
That's all right, Mr. Jenkins.

01:10:59.738 --> 01:11:01.019
I know what I'm doing.

01:11:01.079 --> 01:11:04.481
But it's very late, and you're a long way from plastic.

01:11:04.541 --> 01:11:09.904
Mr. Jenkins, I know how to get back to plastic, so please don't worry about me.

01:11:09.964 --> 01:11:13.446
Well, call me if you need any help, Portia.

01:11:13.506 --> 01:11:14.667
Of course I will.

01:11:14.727 --> 01:11:16.768
Now, go home to Mrs. Jenkins.

01:11:16.828 --> 01:11:17.928
I'll be all right.

01:11:17.988 --> 01:11:21.028
Okay then.

01:11:21.088 --> 01:11:25.718
I can't phone you Mr Jenkins.

01:11:25.778 --> 01:11:33.682
We're in the middle of nowhere, and my cell phone doesn't work.

01:11:33.742 --> 01:11:45.728
Well Sophie, you've done some crazy things in your life, but this...

01:11:45.788 --> 01:11:50.018
Go away!

01:11:50.079 --> 01:11:52.479
And never come near me again!

01:11:52.540 --> 01:11:53.280
Dorothy!

01:11:53.340 --> 01:11:54.630
Go away!

01:11:54.690 --> 01:11:55.511
Dorothy!

01:11:55.571 --> 01:11:56.511
Where are you?

01:11:56.571 --> 01:11:57.752
Let me see you!

01:11:57.812 --> 01:11:59.292
No!

01:11:59.352 --> 01:12:00.142
Dorothy!

01:12:00.202 --> 01:12:01.163
Please!

01:12:01.223 --> 01:12:06.024
Let me see you and let me talk to you!

01:12:06.084 --> 01:12:09.296
Go away!

01:12:09.356 --> 01:12:11.157
Let me talk to you!

01:12:11.177 --> 01:12:12.957
What do you want?

01:12:13.017 --> 01:12:15.006
Dorothy, where are you?

01:12:15.066 --> 01:12:16.584
I'm here.

01:12:16.644 --> 01:12:18.104
By the well.

01:12:18.164 --> 01:12:19.584
Dorothy.

01:12:19.644 --> 01:12:23.136
Just listen to me for a moment.

01:12:23.196 --> 01:12:27.007
You came here because of me.

01:12:27.067 --> 01:12:29.428
How do you know?

01:12:29.488 --> 01:12:32.259
Because I'm...

01:12:32.279 --> 01:12:35.850
I'm much new Ellen.

01:12:35.910 --> 01:12:39.611
Please stop.

01:12:39.671 --> 01:12:42.532
Please, listen to me.

01:12:42.592 --> 01:12:46.616
I didn't know about you until I came here.

01:12:46.676 --> 01:12:51.910
Now I know who you are, and I know the terrible things that happened to you.

01:12:51.970 --> 01:12:54.052
I want to say...

01:12:54.112 --> 01:12:55.413
I don't know.

01:12:55.433 --> 01:12:58.476
I want to say I'm sorry.

01:12:58.496 --> 01:12:59.037
You're sorry.

01:12:59.057 --> 01:13:02.656
You're sorry, Dorothy.

01:13:02.716 --> 01:13:09.366
I want you to forgive my family for the terrible things that were done to you.

01:13:09.426 --> 01:13:12.707
But remember, they were done by my ancestors.

01:13:12.767 --> 01:13:16.059
You can't blame me for that.

01:13:16.079 --> 01:13:19.511
I wish I could do something to stop the pain you feel.

01:13:19.571 --> 01:13:23.193
I wish I could do something to put it right for you.

01:13:23.253 --> 01:13:24.784
And for Ivan.

01:13:24.844 --> 01:13:26.535
Say his name.

01:13:26.594 --> 01:13:27.665
What?

01:13:27.725 --> 01:13:29.526
Say his name.

01:13:29.586 --> 01:13:30.757
Ivan.

01:13:30.817 --> 01:13:32.849
Say it loud.

01:13:32.909 --> 01:13:34.070
Ivan!

01:13:34.130 --> 01:13:35.631
Say it louder!

01:13:35.691 --> 01:13:36.902
Ivan!

01:13:36.962 --> 01:13:39.133
Say it again and again!

01:13:39.193 --> 01:13:40.524
Ivan!

01:13:40.584 --> 01:13:42.114
Ivan!

01:13:42.174 --> 01:13:45.576
Ivan!

01:13:45.636 --> 01:13:48.778
Dorothy!

01:13:48.838 --> 01:13:49.908
Ivan?

01:13:49.968 --> 01:13:51.119
Ivan!

01:13:51.179 --> 01:13:52.400
Where are you?

01:13:52.460 --> 01:13:53.880
I'm here!

01:13:53.940 --> 01:13:55.992
I've been waiting for you!

01:13:56.052 --> 01:13:57.312
Ivan!

01:13:57.372 --> 01:14:00.364
Thank God I found you!

01:14:00.424 --> 01:14:06.561
Oh my God!

01:14:06.620 --> 01:14:12.968
Jesus, my phone's working.

01:14:13.028 --> 01:14:13.918
Hello?

01:14:13.978 --> 01:14:16.070
Sophie, are you all right?

01:14:16.130 --> 01:14:17.131
Yes.

01:14:17.192 --> 01:14:18.352
Good.

01:14:18.412 --> 01:14:21.015
So you're back at the house.

01:14:21.075 --> 01:14:23.938
Sophie, where are you?

01:14:23.998 --> 01:14:25.259
Don't worry, Tom.

01:14:25.319 --> 01:14:26.830
I'm all right.

01:14:26.890 --> 01:14:28.892
Everything's all right.

